1
00:00:01,784 --> 00:00:04,748
♪ In the not too distant future ♪

2
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:08,067
♪ Next Sunday AD ♪

3
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:11,032
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

4
00:00:11,032 --> 00:00:14,520
♪ Not too different than you or me ♪

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,699
♪ He worked in a satellite loading bay ♪

6
00:00:17,699 --> 00:00:20,872
♪ Just polishing switches to pay his way ♪

7
00:00:20,872 --> 00:00:23,544
♪ He did his job with
the a cheerful face ♪

8
00:00:23,544 --> 00:00:25,144
♪ But his bosses didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:25,144 --> 00:00:29,992
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

10
00:00:29,992 --> 00:00:33,304
♪ With seven cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:33,304 --> 00:00:36,312
♪ The worst ever made ♪

12
00:00:36,312 --> 00:00:39,486
♪ Joel says when you got lemons ♪

13
00:00:39,486 --> 00:00:42,669
♪ You make lemonade ♪

14
00:00:42,669 --> 00:00:45,464
♪ Now keep in mind he can't control ♪

15
00:00:45,464 --> 00:00:48,639
♪ When the movies begin or end ♪

16
00:00:48,639 --> 00:00:51,821
♪ Because he used the extra parts ♪

17
00:00:51,821 --> 00:00:56,821
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

18
00:00:56,941 --> 00:01:00,107
♪ Robot roll call Cambot ♪

19
00:01:00,107 --> 00:01:01,107
♪ Servo ♪

20
00:01:01,107 --> 00:01:03,248
♪ Gypsy ♪

21
00:01:03,248 --> 00:01:04,464
♪ Crow ♪

22
00:01:04,464 --> 00:01:07,344
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

23
00:01:07,344 --> 00:01:10,544
♪ And other science facts ♪

24
00:01:10,544 --> 00:01:13,904
♪ Just repeat to yourself
it's just a show ♪

25
00:01:13,904 --> 00:01:17,019
♪ I should really just relax ♪

26
00:01:17,019 --> 00:01:21,269
♪ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♪

27
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:28,044
(vault banging)

28
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:34,510
- Hey, hi, everybody,
my name is Joel Hodgson,

29
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:35,343
this is Crow

30
00:01:35,343 --> 00:01:37,590
and sorry we're on the satellite of love.

31
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:39,250
We're marooned in outer space.

32
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:41,510
Cambot you can bring it in a little bit

33
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:43,056
and it's frustration
'cause it's Thanksgiving.

34
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:44,869
You know, at least we got to see

35
00:01:44,869 --> 00:01:47,900
the Macy's Thanksgiving
Day Parade, you know.

36
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,115
- Yes, I noticed they're still using

37
00:01:49,115 --> 00:01:51,530
that Underdog balloon.

38
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,950
Say, does he get residuals for that?

39
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:57,460
- No, Crow, Underdog
is a cartoon character.

40
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,725
Nobody gets residuals

41
00:01:58,725 --> 00:02:02,160
for being an overinflated caricature

42
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,610
filled with hot air.

43
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:04,853
- What about Geraldo?

44
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:07,460
- Now that's funny.

45
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,378
- It is?
- Yeah.

46
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,211
(Crow laughing)

47
00:02:09,211 --> 00:02:10,240
- Oh, we got movie sign.

48
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,390
Today's movie is "Revenge
of the Mysterons from Mars."

49
00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:15,013
It's filmed in super marionation.

50
00:02:15,013 --> 00:02:16,670
You go through, we gotta go around.

51
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:18,010
Let's cheese it, Crow.

52
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:20,760
(vault creaking)

53
00:02:24,449 --> 00:02:26,949
(grand music)

54
00:02:31,639 --> 00:02:34,639
(suspenseful music)

55
00:02:42,028 --> 00:02:44,471
- [Mysteron] This is a
priority planned mission

56
00:02:44,471 --> 00:02:46,973
to Mysteron Imperial Council.

57
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,040
We have followed standard procedure

58
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,550
in sending our message of good will

59
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:55,120
to the inhabitants of this system,

60
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,860
but they ruthlessly
and without provocation

61
00:02:57,860 --> 00:03:00,520
have attacked our base.

62
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,830
In retaliation for the violent action,

63
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,530
we are launching an attack

64
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,774
that will result in total destruction

65
00:03:07,774 --> 00:03:12,346
of the third planet known as Earth.

66
00:03:12,346 --> 00:03:14,010
(logo hissing)

67
00:03:14,010 --> 00:03:17,010
(suspenseful music)

68
00:04:25,402 --> 00:04:27,985
(gentle music)

69
00:04:28,962 --> 00:04:31,545
(upbeat music)

70
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,980
- [Man] First picture transmission starts

71
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:47,360
in 35 seconds.

72
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:53,993
30 seconds.

73
00:04:53,993 --> 00:04:55,150
- They must have spotted it.

74
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:57,053
What's the flight profile look like?

75
00:04:58,204 --> 00:04:59,280
- It looks like this.
- Right on target.

76
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,530
21,000 miles from Mars.

77
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:02,686
- [Joel] Hey, Crow.

78
00:05:02,686 --> 00:05:04,269
- [Man] 20 seconds.

79
00:05:14,792 --> 00:05:15,891
10 seconds.

80
00:05:15,891 --> 00:05:16,724
Nine.

81
00:05:18,161 --> 00:05:20,911
- [Joel] See what's gonna happen.

82
00:05:22,023 --> 00:05:24,722
(explosion pounding)

83
00:05:24,722 --> 00:05:25,770
- One, zero.

84
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:27,263
Start transmission countdown.

85
00:05:28,127 --> 00:05:31,044
(counter clicking)

86
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,320
- Have we done it?

87
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,380
- We know know for nearly four minutes.

88
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:45,390
Mars is about 43 million miles away.

89
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:47,157
It'll take that long for
the signals to reach us.

90
00:05:47,157 --> 00:05:48,420
- That is if the Mysterons haven't

91
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,973
already destroyed the satellite.

92
00:05:49,973 --> 00:05:51,840
- I'll report to cloud base.

93
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:52,673
- Right.

94
00:05:52,673 --> 00:05:56,370
(suspenseful music)

95
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:57,890
- [Joel] Cloud base.

96
00:05:57,890 --> 00:05:59,711
- What's the latest
situation, Captain Blue?

97
00:05:59,711 --> 00:06:02,130
- We're at K14 observatory.

98
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:04,200
The satellite should have
started transmitting.

99
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,830
We're waiting for the first pictures.

100
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,210
- Thank you, Captain Blue.

101
00:06:07,210 --> 00:06:08,212
Keep me informed.

102
00:06:08,212 --> 00:06:09,463
- SIG, Colonel.

103
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,390
How do you rate our
chances, Captain Scarlet?

104
00:06:12,390 --> 00:06:15,200
- Well, it's hard to
deceive the Mysterons,

105
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,869
but there's always a chance.

106
00:06:16,869 --> 00:06:19,861
(counter clicking)

107
00:06:19,861 --> 00:06:23,680
- Signal to noise ratio 0124
DB, definition positive.

108
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:26,243
- Good.

109
00:06:26,243 --> 00:06:27,120
Check video.

110
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,740
- Video check positive.

111
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:32,630
Beam width and flex density AOI.

112
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:34,510
- Check all primary circuits.

113
00:06:34,510 --> 00:06:38,391
- Computer feed out,
primary circuits, positive.

114
00:06:38,391 --> 00:06:41,308
(counter clicking)

115
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,350
- Well, we'll so now know.

116
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:45,260
Check video.

117
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,093
- I just did.

118
00:06:46,093 --> 00:06:47,980
- [Man] Well, do it again.

119
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:49,404
- It's getting pretty tense.

120
00:06:49,404 --> 00:06:53,244
- Yes, a lot of time and effort
has gone into this project.

121
00:06:53,244 --> 00:06:56,231
No one's had much sleep
these last three days.

122
00:06:56,231 --> 00:06:57,506
- [Joel] Oh, I am.

123
00:06:57,506 --> 00:06:58,624
- [Crow] Now we can
sleep through the movie.

124
00:06:58,624 --> 00:06:59,669
- Signal's still strong.

125
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:00,853
It's not being jammed.

126
00:07:01,801 --> 00:07:04,634
(machine beeping)

127
00:07:07,226 --> 00:07:10,143
(counter clicking)

128
00:07:15,444 --> 00:07:17,042
- [Joel] They got a satellite dish

129
00:07:17,042 --> 00:07:19,209
like you wouldn't believe.

130
00:07:21,521 --> 00:07:23,771
- [Crow] It's only a model.

131
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,473
- [Joel] Somebody just made a pod.

132
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,358
- Close ups of Mars.

133
00:07:30,358 --> 00:07:34,703
43 million miles across
space to that screen.

134
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:41,033
- 20 seconds.

135
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:43,730
Stand by.

136
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:47,123
Start video recording 15 seconds, now.

137
00:07:49,644 --> 00:07:51,330
- Here they come.

138
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:55,923
- [Man] Five, four, three, two.

139
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,040
- We've lost the signal.

140
00:07:59,040 --> 00:07:59,873
- Check it.

141
00:07:59,873 --> 00:08:01,830
- No possible doubt.

142
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:03,720
It's been destroyed two seconds

143
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,620
before the first picture transmission.

144
00:08:08,870 --> 00:08:11,140
- The Mysterons have
destroyed the satellite.

145
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,644
Phase one complete according to planned.

146
00:08:13,644 --> 00:08:16,597
- [Mysterons] This is the
voice of the Mysterons.

147
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:21,533
We know that you can hear us earth men.

148
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:27,720
The eye that dares to look upon our planet

149
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:30,313
has been destroyed.

150
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:35,330
You will never succeed.

151
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:40,330
You will never discover the
secret of the Mysterons.

152
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:45,010
We will be avenged.

153
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:48,410
- [Joel] Feels like
we're really here, Crow.

154
00:08:48,410 --> 00:08:51,414
- [Crow] Wow, it does, ooh.

155
00:08:51,414 --> 00:08:53,940
- Urbinol internal circuits, Leftenant?

156
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:54,773
- Yes, sir.

157
00:08:56,450 --> 00:08:58,060
- Members of Spectrum,

158
00:08:58,060 --> 00:09:00,270
as you have heard the
first satellite launched

159
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:02,650
to orbit Mars and
relayed pictures to earth

160
00:09:02,650 --> 00:09:05,620
has been destroyed by the Mysterons.

161
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:07,690
This was, of course, anticipated

162
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:10,861
and the operation will
continue as planned.

163
00:09:10,861 --> 00:09:11,694
- [Joel] I wonder why they
destroyed the pictures?

164
00:09:11,694 --> 00:09:14,020
- SK14 observatory is at present beyond

165
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:15,780
the range of the Angel aircraft.

166
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,613
- [Crow] You say something?

167
00:09:16,613 --> 00:09:17,830
- Our base will travel immediately

168
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:20,813
to a position 50 miles
west of the observatory

169
00:09:20,813 --> 00:09:22,300
in the Himalayas.

170
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:25,510
From there we will maintain
aerial surveillance.

171
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:28,216
For the next 24 hours,
all Spectrum personnel

172
00:09:28,216 --> 00:09:29,803
are on red alert.

173
00:09:30,648 --> 00:09:34,678
This exercise is part of a
larger plan, Operation Sword

174
00:09:34,678 --> 00:09:38,306
and we must succeed, that is all.

175
00:09:38,306 --> 00:09:40,020
Leftenant Green?

176
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:40,853
- Yes, sir?

177
00:09:40,853 --> 00:09:42,645
- [Colonel White] Start horizontal jets.

178
00:09:42,645 --> 00:09:45,562
(triumphant music)

179
00:10:08,764 --> 00:10:10,464
- Well, looks like we're underway.

180
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,610
- Maximum safe cruise, Colonel.

181
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:14,650
- [Joel] Look at the Jacuzzi he's got.

182
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:16,645
- Set a course 142 magnetic.

183
00:10:16,645 --> 00:10:19,580
And maintain present speed.

184
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,403
Phase two has begun.

185
00:10:26,149 --> 00:10:28,649
(grand music)

186
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,340
- [Joel] Looks like Buck Hale.

187
00:10:34,223 --> 00:10:35,573
- [Crow] They are in space.

188
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:43,020
- [Joel] Look, look.

189
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:45,243
- [Crow] Ooh, what is it?

190
00:10:46,326 --> 00:10:47,212
- [Joel] I hope it's one of ours.

191
00:10:47,212 --> 00:10:49,883
- I have the mini satellite
on an infrared track.

192
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,590
- [Joel] Here it comes again.

193
00:10:55,370 --> 00:10:57,363
- Touch down in two minutes.

194
00:10:58,241 --> 00:11:00,120
- Let's hope the Mysterons
don't detect this one.

195
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,591
- [Joel] Let's hope they
have a strong defense.

196
00:11:01,591 --> 00:11:02,960
- We're tracking them
by infrared reflection

197
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,356
of the sun's rays from
the satellite shell.

198
00:11:05,356 --> 00:11:08,006
At least there's no transmission
for them to pick up.

199
00:11:10,348 --> 00:11:14,370
- [Joel] Uh-oh, flying
meatball 10 o'clock.

200
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,850
- It's working perfecting,
right on target.

201
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:21,190
Minnesat Five is keeping the martian moon

202
00:11:21,190 --> 00:11:23,760
between itself and the Mysterons.

203
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:26,326
- I've got a feeling it's gonna make it.

204
00:11:26,326 --> 00:11:29,326
(suspenseful music)

205
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:38,920
(ship flame crackling)

206
00:11:45,996 --> 00:11:47,650
- The retros are fired.

207
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:49,300
It's altered course as scheduled.

208
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:53,930
(suspenseful music)

209
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,020
- [Joel] It's a transformer.

210
00:12:14,273 --> 00:12:18,900
It's heading straight
for us, oh, look out, oh.

211
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,233
- [Crow] That was a close one.
- [Joel] Oh, yeah.

212
00:12:28,533 --> 00:12:31,521
Kind of looks like Cambot, doesn't it?

213
00:12:31,521 --> 00:12:32,680
- [Crow] It does.

214
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,810
- It's landed.

215
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:34,920
We've done it.

216
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:35,930
- Wonderful.

217
00:12:35,930 --> 00:12:37,750
Well, we've succeeded.

218
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:39,680
We've soft landed a small satellite

219
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,500
on the martian moon Phobus.

220
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:43,520
- And without the Mysterons detecting it.

221
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:47,690
- Right, Phobus orbits Mars
every 7 hours, 40 minutes

222
00:12:47,690 --> 00:12:49,680
and our mini sat will get a free ride

223
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:50,880
right around the planet.

224
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:53,636
Every seven seconds it
will take a photograph.

225
00:12:53,636 --> 00:12:57,326
These will be relayed back
to us at 0300 hours tonight

226
00:12:57,326 --> 00:12:59,250
after its completed on orbit.

227
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:00,540
- Gentlemen, we're about to obtain

228
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:04,180
the best closeup shots of
Mars ever taken by man.

229
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:05,317
We have a lot of work ahead

230
00:13:05,317 --> 00:13:07,840
and I suggest we all get some rest.

231
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:09,930
- Get some sleep as well, Captain Blue.

232
00:13:09,930 --> 00:13:11,710
- I'll take the first watch, right.

233
00:13:11,710 --> 00:13:14,153
- [Joel] Why do you think
they call him Captain Blue?

234
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:17,670
His language?

235
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:18,503
- [Crow] I think so.

236
00:13:18,503 --> 00:13:20,290
I'm amazed they got Carey
Grant to do the voice

237
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:21,390
for this guy (laughs).

238
00:13:23,254 --> 00:13:26,254
(suspenseful music)

239
00:13:43,392 --> 00:13:47,115
(camera shuttering)

240
00:13:47,115 --> 00:13:50,448
- [Joel] See, it's taking pictures Crow.

241
00:13:52,512 --> 00:13:53,614
- [Crow] That's that.

242
00:13:53,614 --> 00:13:56,197
(upbeat music)

243
00:14:13,429 --> 00:14:16,012
(upbeat music)

244
00:14:19,215 --> 00:14:21,798
(gentle music)

245
00:14:25,914 --> 00:14:26,949
- [Joel] They really
keep it clean in there.

246
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:30,390
- [Servo] What's going on here, hmm.

247
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:31,500
- [Joel] Shh.

248
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,000
Come on over here.

249
00:14:34,024 --> 00:14:36,607
(gentle music)

250
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:42,295
(suspenseful music)

251
00:15:11,637 --> 00:15:13,150
- Who's there?

252
00:15:13,150 --> 00:15:14,280
- It's only me.

253
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:15,577
Sorry if I startled you.

254
00:15:15,577 --> 00:15:18,630
- Oh, Dr. Breck, I
thought you were in bed.

255
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,403
- Well, I couldn't sleep.

256
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:22,480
What time is it?

257
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,150
- Nearly midnight.

258
00:15:24,150 --> 00:15:26,320
- Three hours to go.

259
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,940
The night's so clear, may I?

260
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,090
- Go ahead.

261
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:33,090
I was stargazing myself
before you came in.

262
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:34,640
- Mars.

263
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:35,563
The red planet.

264
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:39,868
- [Joel] Seems like a nice enough fellow.

265
00:15:39,868 --> 00:15:40,870
- [Crow] At first.

266
00:15:40,870 --> 00:15:41,703
- It was a brilliant idea to soft land

267
00:15:41,703 --> 00:15:43,120
the mini sat on Phobas.

268
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,820
- Yes, it's course was carefully plotted,

269
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:47,950
so Phobus always shielded
the satellite from Mars.

270
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,810
That's why the Mysterons didn't locate it.

271
00:15:49,810 --> 00:15:50,710
- Yes.

272
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:53,530
- Well, you might say we
worked in the shadow of fear.

273
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:54,363
- Fear?

274
00:15:54,363 --> 00:15:57,693
- Yes, Phobus, the Greek word for fear.

275
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,323
The shadow of fear.

276
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,330
- Everything all right?

277
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,360
- Yes, Captain Blue.

278
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,570
- Well, it's midnight.

279
00:16:05,570 --> 00:16:07,180
I'll take over the watch Captain Scarlet.

280
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:08,833
- Right, I'll get some sleep.

281
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:14,180
- I suggest you get some
rest, as well, Dr. Breck.

282
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:15,770
- All right, Captain, I think I will try

283
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:17,010
and get an hour or so.

284
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:18,340
- I'm gonna check outside.

285
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:19,330
Goodnight.

286
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:20,380
- Goodnight, Captain.

287
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,320
- [Joel] Doesn't Captain Blue look kind

288
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,607
of like Glen Campbell?

289
00:16:28,607 --> 00:16:30,612
- [Crow] A little bit, yes.

290
00:16:30,612 --> 00:16:32,350
- [Joel] A little bit country.

291
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:34,150
- [Crow] A little big rock and roll.

292
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:36,900
- [Servo] He's the purple stone cowboy.

293
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:39,567
(ominous music)

294
00:17:00,757 --> 00:17:01,830
- The light?

295
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:02,663
It's so.

296
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,353
- [Servo] Bright?

297
00:17:04,353 --> 00:17:05,186
- I can't...

298
00:17:06,490 --> 00:17:07,950
I can't...

299
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:10,200
- [Joel] Sounds like?

300
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,250
- Compensating light.

301
00:17:13,090 --> 00:17:14,195
- [Joel] Two syllables.

302
00:17:14,195 --> 00:17:15,293
- [Servo] Shoulda bought a vowel.

303
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:20,329
(ominous music)

304
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:28,023
- [Joel] The Olympics rings.

305
00:17:35,810 --> 00:17:37,566
- [Crow] What big zippers you have.

306
00:17:37,566 --> 00:17:40,066
(Joel laughs)

307
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:45,956
- [Servo] Funny, his legs
don't move like a human.

308
00:17:45,956 --> 00:17:48,956
(suspenseful music)

309
00:17:56,606 --> 00:17:57,856
- [Joel] Uh-oh.

310
00:18:02,490 --> 00:18:04,103
- Dr. Breck, are you all right?

311
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:08,853
- Fine, Captain, I'm fine.

312
00:18:10,350 --> 00:18:13,270
- [Joel] Dr. Breck, the
shampoo genius, that's it.

313
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:15,380
- [Crow] He does have nice hair.

314
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:16,573
- What's our position, Leftenant Green?

315
00:18:16,573 --> 00:18:20,030
- We're over flying the
Himalayas about eight miles west

316
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:21,170
of the observatory.

317
00:18:21,170 --> 00:18:22,194
- Time?

318
00:18:22,194 --> 00:18:23,900
- [Leftenant Green] 0158.

319
00:18:23,900 --> 00:18:25,660
- Just over an hour to go.

320
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,660
Right, Leftenant.

321
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:27,883
Launch all angels.

322
00:18:28,830 --> 00:18:30,843
- Angel One, immediate launch.

323
00:18:36,008 --> 00:18:38,425
(jet firing)

324
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:44,393
Angels Two Three, immediate launch.

325
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,770
- [Servo] That must be Charlie.

326
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:53,850
- Maintain arrow
surveillance as instructed.

327
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:58,034
Observe radio silence
except in an emergency.

328
00:18:58,034 --> 00:19:00,617
(jet whirring)

329
00:19:04,584 --> 00:19:07,267
- [Joel] There it goes.

330
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:09,240
- All Angels sky born, sir.

331
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,350
- All we can do now wait.

332
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:13,053
The rest is up to the astronomers.

333
00:19:16,670 --> 00:19:18,720
- Gone? He can't have gone.

334
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,860
I've looked everywhere.

335
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:21,470
- He's not in the observatory.

336
00:19:21,470 --> 00:19:23,160
He just be found.

337
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,310
There's less than an
hour before transmission.

338
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:27,110
- His bed hasn't been slept in.

339
00:19:27,110 --> 00:19:29,660
Dr. Breck is definitely
not in the building.

340
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:31,060
- I don't like it.

341
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:32,300
We're so close to success,

342
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:34,193
nothing must go wrong.

343
00:19:35,872 --> 00:19:36,980
- [Servo] We've got
another hour and a half

344
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,653
to the movie, something has to.

345
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,000
- [Joel] Rotation gear housing.

346
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,377
It's filled with hula hoops, right?

347
00:19:54,263 --> 00:19:56,351
- [Servo] You a cut up.

348
00:19:56,351 --> 00:19:59,018
(ominous music)

349
00:20:07,993 --> 00:20:09,493
- [Joel] It's the bubble bomb.

350
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:14,190
- [Servo] Do you want to
see my impression of that.

351
00:20:17,124 --> 00:20:18,774
- [Joel] Hey, that's pretty good.

352
00:20:20,370 --> 00:20:22,163
- [Servo] Thank you, I've been practicing.

353
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,490
- That's the position, Colonel

354
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:27,780
and there's less than 40 minutes to go.

355
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:30,950
- Breck is almost certainly
in the hands of the Mysterons.

356
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:32,757
But we must go ahead with the project.

357
00:20:32,757 --> 00:20:35,370
I will order the spectrum
helicopter to fly

358
00:20:35,370 --> 00:20:37,215
as low as possible over the area

359
00:20:37,215 --> 00:20:39,610
in the hope that it may spot him.

360
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:41,580
Meantime, carry on with the preparations

361
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,452
for the transmission.

362
00:20:42,452 --> 00:20:43,700
- Sig.

363
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,180
He can't have gone far Captain Blue.

364
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:47,300
We'll go outside and try and find him.

365
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:50,847
- Come Antolini, let's
get to the computer.

366
00:20:50,847 --> 00:20:53,514
(ship whirring)

367
00:20:58,847 --> 00:21:02,601
- [Crow] That's a
helicopter, not a computer.

368
00:21:02,601 --> 00:21:05,601
(suspenseful music)

369
00:21:07,010 --> 00:21:08,510
- I'm glad there's a moon.

370
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:09,343
- That's for sure.

371
00:21:09,343 --> 00:21:12,283
Let's get a Mysteron
detector from the SPV.

372
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:17,003
- Test transmission in 10 seconds.

373
00:21:21,930 --> 00:21:26,203
Five, four, three, zero.

374
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:36,580
- Bang on the nose, we're in business.

375
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:38,830
- Did you get a fix on the
beam width and flex density?

376
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:40,109
- Yes.

377
00:21:40,109 --> 00:21:43,130
But we'll have to move the
aerial point 12 degrees.

378
00:21:43,130 --> 00:21:44,390
- Right.

379
00:21:44,390 --> 00:21:45,830
- We wait till the last minute

380
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:47,600
Just in case the Mysterons are trying

381
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:49,043
to pinpoint our position.

382
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:53,120
- He could be anywhere.

383
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,980
- Right, we better keep looking.

384
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,226
Time is running out.

385
00:21:56,226 --> 00:21:59,226
(suspenseful music)

386
00:22:00,630 --> 00:22:02,487
- Start transmission countdown.

387
00:22:03,744 --> 00:22:06,661
(counter clicking)

388
00:22:24,183 --> 00:22:26,706
- [Joel] Can you imagine all the stations.

389
00:22:26,706 --> 00:22:29,706
(suspenseful music)

390
00:22:32,151 --> 00:22:34,180
- That could be him.

391
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:38,444
- Captain Sky, I think
Captain Gray has located them.

392
00:22:38,444 --> 00:22:41,444
We're going around for another look.

393
00:22:46,466 --> 00:22:48,299
- [Servo] Ooh, doggie.

394
00:23:00,542 --> 00:23:02,779
- Yes, we found him.

395
00:23:02,779 --> 00:23:05,065
He's in the rocks about the observatory.

396
00:23:05,065 --> 00:23:06,280
- SIG Melody.

397
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:09,260
Well, Captain Blue, he's
in the rocks of Phobas.

398
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,569
- Let's go.

399
00:23:10,569 --> 00:23:11,763
- Check video.

400
00:23:11,763 --> 00:23:13,395
- Video positive.

401
00:23:13,395 --> 00:23:16,312
(counter clicking)

402
00:23:19,170 --> 00:23:23,102
We'll traverse the area at
transmission minus 40 seconds.

403
00:23:23,102 --> 00:23:26,019
(triumphant music)

404
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:35,880
- Breck.

405
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:37,380
We know you're up there Breck.

406
00:23:41,150 --> 00:23:43,443
All right, we're coming to take you.

407
00:23:45,083 --> 00:23:46,449
(gun firing)

408
00:23:46,449 --> 00:23:49,532
- [Servo] Ooh, they got me, ooh, ooh.

409
00:23:52,142 --> 00:23:53,390
Sorry.

410
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:55,620
- Don't be stupid, Breck.

411
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:57,520
Give up before it's too late.

412
00:23:57,520 --> 00:24:01,190
- It's already too late for you earthmen.

413
00:24:01,190 --> 00:24:02,700
- What does that mean?

414
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:04,100
- I've planted a bomb in

415
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:07,040
the radio telescope's rotation gear.

416
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:09,420
When it's turned, the observatory

417
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:11,093
will be blown to pieces.

418
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,267
You will never beat us.

419
00:24:14,267 --> 00:24:17,222
(gun firing)

420
00:24:17,222 --> 00:24:18,055
- Ah!

421
00:24:18,949 --> 00:24:20,337
- [Crow] (laughing) He got him.

422
00:24:20,337 --> 00:24:21,810
- We've got to warn them.
- There's no time.

423
00:24:21,810 --> 00:24:22,973
- We must try.

424
00:24:23,860 --> 00:24:26,450
- [Joel] You know that
puppet does his own stunts.

425
00:24:26,450 --> 00:24:27,650
- [Crow] Does he really?

426
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:31,116
- Stand by to rotate aerials.

427
00:24:31,116 --> 00:24:32,500
- [Cambot] I personally don't believe

428
00:24:32,500 --> 00:24:34,572
that puppets should be on TV.

429
00:24:34,572 --> 00:24:38,110
(suspenseful music)

430
00:24:38,110 --> 00:24:38,993
- Five seconds.

431
00:24:43,483 --> 00:24:45,536
Rotate aerial.

432
00:24:45,536 --> 00:24:47,286
- [Crow] Don't do it.

433
00:24:54,656 --> 00:24:57,739
- Picture transmission in 30 seconds.

434
00:25:02,208 --> 00:25:04,512
- [Crow] Well, that's a list a thing bomb.

435
00:25:04,512 --> 00:25:07,012
- This time we're gonna do it.

436
00:25:08,118 --> 00:25:10,202
- [Servo] Ooh, doggie.

437
00:25:10,202 --> 00:25:13,285
(building exploding)

438
00:25:59,251 --> 00:26:02,001
(doors slamming)

439
00:26:04,970 --> 00:26:05,803
- Okay, come here.

440
00:26:05,803 --> 00:26:06,970
Hey, Gypsy, come on over here,

441
00:26:06,970 --> 00:26:08,030
yeah, come here.

442
00:26:08,030 --> 00:26:10,269
Okay, do you see these gourds I got here.

443
00:26:10,269 --> 00:26:11,102
- Yeah?

444
00:26:11,102 --> 00:26:12,051
- Okay, now these gourds

445
00:26:12,051 --> 00:26:14,963
are what we usually put
in a cornucopia, okay?

446
00:26:14,963 --> 00:26:15,965
Back on earth.

447
00:26:15,965 --> 00:26:16,798
- A cornucopia?

448
00:26:16,798 --> 00:26:18,419
- Yeah, a cornucopia is this thing,

449
00:26:18,419 --> 00:26:20,465
it's kind of shaped like a horn,

450
00:26:20,465 --> 00:26:22,763
like you're not getting this are you.

451
00:26:22,763 --> 00:26:24,700
Wait a minute, just come on over here,

452
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:25,730
put your head down.

453
00:26:25,730 --> 00:26:27,550
Can I use your mouth to demonstrate

454
00:26:27,550 --> 00:26:28,650
what a cornucopia is?

455
00:26:28,650 --> 00:26:29,720
- A cornucopia?

456
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:30,700
- Yeah, a cornucopia.

457
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:34,080
It's also known, just open
your mouth us, that's good.

458
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:35,949
It's also known as a horn of plenty.

459
00:26:35,949 --> 00:26:38,579
And around Thanksgiving time on Earth

460
00:26:38,579 --> 00:26:40,701
we take these horn of plenties

461
00:26:40,701 --> 00:26:43,368
and fill them up with
gourds and put them around

462
00:26:43,368 --> 00:26:44,470
kind of as a centerpiece.

463
00:26:44,470 --> 00:26:45,463
- A centerpiece?

464
00:26:46,340 --> 00:26:49,280
- Yeah, to show people
that it's been a good year,

465
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,387
that we've had plenty.

466
00:26:52,340 --> 00:26:55,300
I think you're starting
to get it, you know that?

467
00:26:55,300 --> 00:26:56,500
- Hello, Joel Hodgson.

468
00:26:56,500 --> 00:26:57,383
- Hey, Crow.

469
00:26:57,383 --> 00:27:00,560
- Giving Gypsum another one
of your famous food revs.

470
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,550
- No, good one Crow.

471
00:27:02,550 --> 00:27:05,240
You're getting better, no,
it's nothing like that.

472
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:09,195
I'm making Gypsum's mouth
into a horn of plenty.

473
00:27:09,195 --> 00:27:10,140
- Oh.

474
00:27:10,140 --> 00:27:12,520
- It's a way of showing on earth

475
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:13,589
that we've had enough.

476
00:27:13,589 --> 00:27:16,140
(Gypsum squealing)

477
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:17,256
- I think Gypsum just invented

478
00:27:17,256 --> 00:27:19,690
a way to show she's had enough.

479
00:27:19,690 --> 00:27:20,818
- Right?

480
00:27:20,818 --> 00:27:21,651
Are you okay?

481
00:27:21,651 --> 00:27:26,140
Okay, we're gonna break
for a commercial now.

482
00:27:26,140 --> 00:27:29,513
Why don't you go make a sandwich
or something? All right.

483
00:27:30,704 --> 00:27:33,287
(upbeat music)

484
00:27:51,067 --> 00:27:53,650
(upbeat music)

485
00:27:57,804 --> 00:28:00,804
(satellite beeping)

486
00:28:21,424 --> 00:28:22,955
- [Servo] Mm, those
commercials were pretty good.

487
00:28:22,955 --> 00:28:26,859
- K14 observatory has
been completely destroyed.

488
00:28:26,859 --> 00:28:29,259
There is no chance of
there being any survivors.

489
00:28:33,570 --> 00:28:34,770
- [Joel] Jackie Gleason.

490
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:42,980
- This is lunar control.
- You see his face?

491
00:28:42,980 --> 00:28:45,320
- [Colonel White] Since man's
first successful landing

492
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:47,663
on the moon back in the 1970s,

493
00:28:48,530 --> 00:28:50,460
we have gradually learn to live

494
00:28:50,460 --> 00:28:51,809
on this barren, apparently
uninviting world-

495
00:28:51,809 --> 00:28:54,963
- 1970s?
- In safety and comfort.

496
00:28:55,990 --> 00:28:59,260
- At present, there are some
4,000 men and women living

497
00:28:59,260 --> 00:29:01,942
and working on the lunar service.

498
00:29:01,942 --> 00:29:05,430
The earth is engaged in
a savage war of nerves

499
00:29:05,430 --> 00:29:07,170
with the Mysterons.

500
00:29:07,170 --> 00:29:08,810
This is none of our doing

501
00:29:08,810 --> 00:29:11,060
and we want no part of it.

502
00:29:11,060 --> 00:29:13,590
I wish to announce that I have been able

503
00:29:13,590 --> 00:29:17,460
to contact the Mysterons,
to communicate with them

504
00:29:17,460 --> 00:29:20,350
and come to a peaceful settlement.

505
00:29:20,350 --> 00:29:22,450
This is not our fight.

506
00:29:22,450 --> 00:29:24,511
The moon does not take sides,

507
00:29:24,511 --> 00:29:26,806
but we will not support the earth

508
00:29:26,806 --> 00:29:28,313
against the Mysterons.

509
00:29:29,390 --> 00:29:30,740
How was the transmission?

510
00:29:30,740 --> 00:29:31,990
- It seemed fine.

511
00:29:31,990 --> 00:29:33,133
Ask the computer, sir.

512
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:39,800
- [Colonel White] How was
the transmission, SID?

513
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:43,250
- [SID] Transmission strength
and definition excellent.

514
00:29:43,250 --> 00:29:47,623
Predict reception around the
moon and on earth exceptional.

515
00:29:50,650 --> 00:29:53,023
- [Servo] That sounded like
my second grade teacher.

516
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,790
- Members of Spectrum.

517
00:29:55,790 --> 00:29:58,550
You have all heard or read
last night's transmission

518
00:29:58,550 --> 00:29:59,990
by the lunar controller

519
00:29:59,990 --> 00:30:01,280
in which he declared the moon

520
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:02,980
an independent world.

521
00:30:02,980 --> 00:30:05,650
- Is he legally entitled
to do this, Colonel?

522
00:30:05,650 --> 00:30:06,780
- We're not concerned with the legality

523
00:30:06,780 --> 00:30:08,901
of the situation, Captain.

524
00:30:08,901 --> 00:30:09,902
The Spectrum's main purpose

525
00:30:09,902 --> 00:30:12,240
is to counter the Mysteron threat.

526
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:14,270
That is our basic function.

527
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:16,240
One part of the lunar
controller's announcement

528
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:18,277
was to particular significance.

529
00:30:18,277 --> 00:30:20,990
Leftenant Green will read
the relevant section.

530
00:30:20,990 --> 00:30:24,440
- Holt, I have been able
to contact the Mysterons.

531
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:26,450
- [Joel] Hey, is that a
Grateful Dead pin he's got on.

532
00:30:26,450 --> 00:30:29,287
- To counter peaceful settlement and port.

533
00:30:29,287 --> 00:30:33,030
- [Servo] I think it is.
- Can we believe what he says?

534
00:30:33,030 --> 00:30:33,863
- [Crow] And that looks
bad about the shoulders.

535
00:30:33,863 --> 00:30:35,106
- I don't know, Captain Blue.

536
00:30:35,106 --> 00:30:36,940
But I do know that we cannot afford

537
00:30:36,940 --> 00:30:38,383
to disbelieve it.

538
00:30:39,470 --> 00:30:40,890
The Spectrum would be very interested

539
00:30:40,890 --> 00:30:43,550
to come to terms with the Mysterons.

540
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:47,080
If the lunar controller has
succeeded, we want to know how.

541
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:48,310
If he hasn't, we want to know

542
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:50,040
the reason for his deception.

543
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:52,350
- Could he be a Mysteron agent, sir?

544
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:53,883
- This cannot be ruled out, Captain.

545
00:30:53,883 --> 00:30:56,226
- [Joel] Doesn't he look
like "The Man from Glad?"

546
00:30:56,226 --> 00:30:57,098
- But there is only one place
we will find the answer.

547
00:30:57,098 --> 00:30:58,100
- [Crow] Nice hair, buddy.

548
00:30:58,100 --> 00:30:59,530
- In Lunarville Seven.

549
00:30:59,530 --> 00:31:02,280
(dramatic music)

550
00:31:06,736 --> 00:31:08,362
- [Man] T-minus 10.

551
00:31:08,362 --> 00:31:10,770
- XK5 to control.

552
00:31:10,770 --> 00:31:12,850
Internal countdown complete.

553
00:31:12,850 --> 00:31:15,680
Five, four, three, two, one, zero.

554
00:31:20,610 --> 00:31:22,210
- Stand by for liftoff.

555
00:31:22,210 --> 00:31:24,660
- [Servo] This movie needs
more countdowns in it.

556
00:31:26,474 --> 00:31:27,724
I just cannot get enough.

557
00:31:29,587 --> 00:31:32,297
(base exploding)

558
00:31:32,297 --> 00:31:33,130
Joel?

559
00:31:35,134 --> 00:31:35,967
Joel?

560
00:31:35,967 --> 00:31:36,800
- [Joel] What?

561
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:37,633
- [Servo] How come you gave me such

562
00:31:37,633 --> 00:31:39,980
a funny voice when you made me?

563
00:31:39,980 --> 00:31:42,263
- [Joel] It reminded me of
my second grade teacher.

564
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:44,180
- [Servo] Good answer, Joel.

565
00:31:44,180 --> 00:31:45,510
- Hike 20,000 feet.

566
00:31:45,510 --> 00:31:46,913
- [Joel] Hey, nice hat, guy.

567
00:31:48,830 --> 00:31:52,130
- Speed 6.5 miles per second.

568
00:31:52,130 --> 00:31:53,173
Escape velocity.

569
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,230
- Well, we're on our way.

570
00:31:55,230 --> 00:31:56,703
- SIG, Captain Scarlet.

571
00:31:57,570 --> 00:31:59,930
We are leaving the earth's atmosphere.

572
00:31:59,930 --> 00:32:02,457
Accelerate to 100,000 MPH.

573
00:32:02,457 --> 00:32:05,207
(dramatic music)

574
00:32:07,958 --> 00:32:09,020
- [Joel] Boy, that moon looks

575
00:32:09,020 --> 00:32:10,936
like Jackie Gleason, doesn't it?

576
00:32:10,936 --> 00:32:12,269
- [Crow] Mm-hmm.

577
00:32:13,910 --> 00:32:17,970
- Colonel White, XK3 is
in orbit around the moon.

578
00:32:17,970 --> 00:32:20,430
Lunar rocket separation in four minutes.

579
00:32:20,430 --> 00:32:21,420
- Right.

580
00:32:21,420 --> 00:32:23,466
Put me in direct contact
with Captain Scarlet.

581
00:32:23,466 --> 00:32:24,299
- Sig.

582
00:32:25,689 --> 00:32:27,630
- This is Colonel White.

583
00:32:27,630 --> 00:32:28,463
As the lunar controller
has banned personal radios

584
00:32:29,657 --> 00:32:30,979
nor other equipment, I'll give you

585
00:32:30,979 --> 00:32:33,550
your final instructions now.

586
00:32:33,550 --> 00:32:34,800
- [Man] Yes, Colonel.

587
00:32:34,800 --> 00:32:37,350
- We have reports that a
new unauthorized complex

588
00:32:37,350 --> 00:32:38,937
is being constructed in the Humbalt Sea

589
00:32:38,937 --> 00:32:41,090
on the far side of the moon.

590
00:32:41,090 --> 00:32:42,700
This must be investigated.

591
00:32:42,700 --> 00:32:44,220
- I have the map reference, sir.

592
00:32:44,220 --> 00:32:45,880
We'll do everything possible.

593
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,256
- I don't have to tell you how important

594
00:32:47,256 --> 00:32:49,260
this assignment is.

595
00:32:49,260 --> 00:32:52,181
The future of the world
may well be in your hands.

596
00:32:52,181 --> 00:32:53,422
Do you all understand?

597
00:32:53,422 --> 00:32:54,762
- [Servo] Look, Joel, I'm a lever.

598
00:32:54,762 --> 00:32:55,595
- Sig.

599
00:32:55,595 --> 00:32:56,428
- [Colonel White] Captain, Blue?

600
00:32:56,428 --> 00:32:57,269
- Sig.

601
00:32:57,269 --> 00:32:58,102
- [Colonel White] Captain Scarlet.

602
00:32:58,102 --> 00:32:58,935
- Sig.

603
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:06,950
- [SID] The Spectrum
personnel in the moon rocket

604
00:33:06,950 --> 00:33:09,440
have left the parking orbit.

605
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:12,283
They will dock as they
agree in four minutes.

606
00:33:13,150 --> 00:33:14,427
- Thank you, SID.

607
00:33:14,427 --> 00:33:16,390
- Go and meet them Orson.

608
00:33:16,390 --> 00:33:19,060
This is their first visit to the moon.

609
00:33:19,060 --> 00:33:21,580
- And their last, Controller?

610
00:33:21,580 --> 00:33:24,672
- Yes, Orson, it could well be their last.

611
00:33:24,672 --> 00:33:27,339
(Joel laughing)

612
00:33:28,691 --> 00:33:31,358
(ominous music)

613
00:33:37,989 --> 00:33:41,822
- [Joel] Oh, Charles,
get away from the blast.

614
00:33:42,990 --> 00:33:44,490
- Let's get into the air lock.

615
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:52,173
- [Servo] Get it, Joe, get it.

616
00:33:58,623 --> 00:34:00,180
- [Man] The walkway is in position.

617
00:34:00,180 --> 00:34:01,560
Open the outer door.

618
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:03,173
- Right, opening now.

619
00:34:06,090 --> 00:34:07,400
- My name's Orson.

620
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:09,170
I'm the lunar controller's PA.

621
00:34:09,170 --> 00:34:10,840
- We would like to see
the lunar controller

622
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:12,100
as soon as possible.

623
00:34:12,100 --> 00:34:13,840
- I'll take you to him immediately.

624
00:34:13,840 --> 00:34:15,640
Please wear these recognition discs.

625
00:34:17,567 --> 00:34:20,317
(dramatic music)

626
00:34:21,470 --> 00:34:24,430
- May I welcome you to Lunarville Seven.

627
00:34:24,430 --> 00:34:27,120
- Thank you, sir, we're glad to be here.

628
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:30,330
- You have already met my personal aid.

629
00:34:30,330 --> 00:34:33,190
Let me introduce our control computer.

630
00:34:33,190 --> 00:34:35,070
His code name is SID.

631
00:34:35,070 --> 00:34:37,590
Speech Intelligence Decoder.

632
00:34:37,590 --> 00:34:41,140
He is programmed to understand
and obey verbal instructions

633
00:34:41,140 --> 00:34:44,010
and can answer with his
own simulated voice.

634
00:34:44,010 --> 00:34:45,230
Say hello, Sid.

635
00:34:45,230 --> 00:34:47,711
- [SID] Good day, Captain Scarlet.

636
00:34:47,711 --> 00:34:49,623
- [Servo] Oh, hello SID.

637
00:34:49,623 --> 00:34:52,610
- [SID] Good day, Leftenant Green.

638
00:34:52,610 --> 00:34:55,060
- He recognizes you by
the badges you're wearing.

639
00:34:55,910 --> 00:34:58,010
Ask him a question, go ahead.

640
00:34:58,010 --> 00:35:00,094
- What is the outside temperature?

641
00:35:00,094 --> 00:35:05,094
- [SID] 2 degrees centigrade,
35.6 degrees Fahrenheit,

642
00:35:05,684 --> 00:35:09,000
275.16 absolute.

643
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,150
- Very thorough.

644
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:13,140
- Yes, SID controls
everything in Lunarville.

645
00:35:13,140 --> 00:35:17,140
The air conditioning, air
locks, power supplies, even-

646
00:35:17,140 --> 00:35:17,973
- [Servo] The plot.

647
00:35:17,973 --> 00:35:19,200
- The rockets and moon mobiles.

648
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:21,020
- A very important piece of equipment.

649
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:24,630
- Assembled entirely on the
moon by our own technicians.

650
00:35:24,630 --> 00:35:27,160
- But designed and developed on earth.

651
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,600
- The earth may have helped us,

652
00:35:28,600 --> 00:35:30,840
but now we are self-reliant, democratic

653
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:32,543
and free, understand.

654
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:36,923
- Well, forgive me gentlemen.

655
00:35:38,380 --> 00:35:39,243
- He's kind of tight.
- Yes.

656
00:35:39,243 --> 00:35:42,910
- I was told you have a message
from the world president.

657
00:35:42,910 --> 00:35:44,800
- Yes, sir, they asked me to hand you

658
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:45,970
this letter personally.

659
00:35:45,970 --> 00:35:47,410
- [Crow] It's from Ed McMahon.

660
00:35:47,410 --> 00:35:49,616
- I'll study it and give you my answer.

661
00:35:49,616 --> 00:35:51,420
- [Servo] You may have already won.

662
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:52,782
- [Man] Please ask Orson.

663
00:35:52,782 --> 00:35:54,728
- Gentlemen, I'm at your service.

664
00:35:54,728 --> 00:35:56,733
- As this is our first visit,

665
00:35:56,733 --> 00:35:59,700
we would appreciate a trip
out on the lunar surface.

666
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:00,861
- [Man] Certainly, SID.

667
00:36:00,861 --> 00:36:01,784
- [Servo] Right this way.

668
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:02,913
- [SID] Yes, Mr. Orson.

669
00:36:02,913 --> 00:36:04,200
- Have a moon mobile ready

670
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:05,490
at air lock number three immediately.

671
00:36:05,490 --> 00:36:08,191
- [SID] The moon mobile will be available

672
00:36:08,191 --> 00:36:10,777
at air lock three at once.

673
00:36:10,777 --> 00:36:12,527
- If you will follow me, gentlemen.

674
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:19,423
- [Crow] This should be good.

675
00:36:24,070 --> 00:36:25,840
- Please fasten your safety belts.

676
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:27,295
The unusual most can be disturbing

677
00:36:27,295 --> 00:36:28,695
until you become used to it.

678
00:36:37,860 --> 00:36:39,160
- [Servo] That is unusual.

679
00:36:42,356 --> 00:36:45,273
(aircraft hissing)

680
00:37:06,068 --> 00:37:11,068
- [Joel] Looks like
it's running out of gas.

681
00:37:12,916 --> 00:37:13,844
- [Crow] Oh, give me a break.

682
00:37:13,844 --> 00:37:15,103
- It's certainly a novel
method of transportation

683
00:37:15,103 --> 00:37:17,053
and surprisingly smooth.

684
00:37:18,210 --> 00:37:19,516
- The earth's gravity
is six times stronger

685
00:37:19,516 --> 00:37:21,170
than the moons'.

686
00:37:21,170 --> 00:37:23,420
A machine like this would
be useless on earth.

687
00:37:23,420 --> 00:37:26,010
The force of impact on
landing would be too great.

688
00:37:26,010 --> 00:37:28,223
- Look, another lunar station.

689
00:37:29,130 --> 00:37:30,430
- Lunarville four.

690
00:37:30,430 --> 00:37:31,620
Most of our food is grown there.

691
00:37:31,620 --> 00:37:34,560
- That must use a great deal of water.

692
00:37:34,560 --> 00:37:36,407
The moon has no natural water.

693
00:37:36,407 --> 00:37:38,610
But first all supplies were
transported from earth.

694
00:37:38,610 --> 00:37:41,343
But the component elements,
hydrogen and oxygen.

695
00:37:41,343 --> 00:37:43,480
- [Crow] And cheese.

696
00:37:43,480 --> 00:37:45,660
- We can now synthesize more than enough

697
00:37:45,660 --> 00:37:47,070
for our own needs.

698
00:37:47,070 --> 00:37:47,940
- Let's see.

699
00:37:47,940 --> 00:37:49,243
If I remember the map correctly,

700
00:37:49,243 --> 00:37:52,550
our present course would
take us to the Humbalt Sea.

701
00:37:52,550 --> 00:37:54,480
- What is your interest in that area?

702
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:56,520
- Oh, a natural curiosity.

703
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:57,840
- It's on the far side of the moon,

704
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,020
never visible from earth.

705
00:37:59,020 --> 00:38:00,550
- And it's 200 miles away.

706
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:01,610
- We have plenty of time.

707
00:38:01,610 --> 00:38:02,570
- I'm afraid not.

708
00:38:02,570 --> 00:38:04,020
- We would appreciate.
- No.

709
00:38:05,420 --> 00:38:07,803
- I'm sorry, maybe another time.

710
00:38:08,670 --> 00:38:09,770
It's late.

711
00:38:09,770 --> 00:38:11,027
We should return to Lunarville Seven.

712
00:38:11,027 --> 00:38:12,593
- [Servo] Something is afoot.

713
00:38:15,195 --> 00:38:20,195
- [Crow] I think it's the
thing on the end of your leg.

714
00:38:22,437 --> 00:38:25,203
- [Servo] You sure are
funny for an ugly robot.

715
00:38:35,654 --> 00:38:36,654
I love that.

716
00:38:39,710 --> 00:38:42,510
- This will be your suite for
the duration of your stay.

717
00:38:44,260 --> 00:38:46,360
- [Joel] Looks like a George Jetson house.

718
00:38:50,380 --> 00:38:52,280
- [Servo] Jane, stop this crazy thing.

719
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:58,270
- [Captain Scarlet] I'm sure
we'll be most comfortable.

720
00:38:58,270 --> 00:38:59,207
- I'll leave you then.

721
00:38:59,207 --> 00:39:00,990
You must be tired.

722
00:39:00,990 --> 00:39:02,250
If the earth light is too bright,

723
00:39:02,250 --> 00:39:04,900
the control for the polarity
window is near the door.

724
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:08,520
- Did you notice his reaction

725
00:39:08,520 --> 00:39:10,070
when you mentioned the Humbalt Sea?

726
00:39:10,070 --> 00:39:11,290
- He bolted.

727
00:39:11,290 --> 00:39:13,850
I think I'll just take a look around.

728
00:39:13,850 --> 00:39:16,663
The room is probably bugged, keep talking.

729
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:19,070
- You know I found that trip

730
00:39:19,070 --> 00:39:21,470
in the moon mobile most interesting.

731
00:39:21,470 --> 00:39:24,100
I never realized how
complex the installations

732
00:39:24,100 --> 00:39:24,933
are on the moon.

733
00:39:24,933 --> 00:39:25,766
- [Servo] It's down here, it's down here.

734
00:39:25,766 --> 00:39:27,107
- [Leftenant Scarlet]
Leftenant Green, do you agree?

735
00:39:27,107 --> 00:39:30,798
- Yes, the synthesis of water
from its component elements

736
00:39:30,798 --> 00:39:33,110
must have been a great breakthrough.

737
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:34,530
- How many people do you think the moon

738
00:39:34,530 --> 00:39:35,726
is capable of supporting?

739
00:39:35,726 --> 00:39:37,859
- [Leftenant Green] Well,
all the elements vital

740
00:39:37,859 --> 00:39:38,787
to human life

741
00:39:38,787 --> 00:39:42,220
are found on or near the lunar surface,

742
00:39:42,220 --> 00:39:44,600
so I think the number is very high.

743
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:46,463
- I think I found it, keep quiet.

744
00:39:56,770 --> 00:39:57,962
- Good night Orson.

745
00:39:57,962 --> 00:39:59,045
- [Orson] Ah!

746
00:40:00,180 --> 00:40:01,610
- Right, I think we can now discuss

747
00:40:01,610 --> 00:40:04,110
the situation without being overheard.

748
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,450
- [Joel] Who says puppets don't have

749
00:40:05,450 --> 00:40:06,283
a sense of humor.
- What is it Orson?

750
00:40:06,283 --> 00:40:07,195
- Scarlet discovered the microphone.

751
00:40:07,195 --> 00:40:08,752
- [Servo] I would never day that.

752
00:40:08,752 --> 00:40:11,504
- Let them make their futile plans.

753
00:40:11,504 --> 00:40:15,203
I have programmed SID to
accept only my authorization.

754
00:40:16,210 --> 00:40:18,443
He will keep all exits sealed.

755
00:40:19,420 --> 00:40:20,693
Let them plot Orson.

756
00:40:21,550 --> 00:40:24,581
They're trapped on Lunarville Seven.

757
00:40:24,581 --> 00:40:27,133
We will deal with them at our leisure.

758
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:34,902
- [Servo] Maybe after a Jacuzzi.

759
00:40:34,902 --> 00:40:37,652
(dramatic music)

760
00:41:13,966 --> 00:41:15,570
- [SID] Who is there?

761
00:41:15,570 --> 00:41:19,090
Identify yourself or I
must sound the alarm.

762
00:41:19,090 --> 00:41:20,653
- I am Captain Scarlet.

763
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:24,560
- [SID] Thank you, Captain Scarlet.

764
00:41:24,560 --> 00:41:25,860
Can I help you?

765
00:41:25,860 --> 00:41:28,100
- I require a moon mobile immediately.

766
00:41:28,100 --> 00:41:30,800
- [SID] I am sorry, your recognition disc

767
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:32,651
cannot authorize a moon mobile.

768
00:41:32,651 --> 00:41:33,948
- Well, who has the authority?

769
00:41:33,948 --> 00:41:36,270
- [SID] In the present emergency,

770
00:41:36,270 --> 00:41:38,016
only the lunar controller.

771
00:41:38,016 --> 00:41:39,147
- Emergency?

772
00:41:39,147 --> 00:41:40,811
- [SID] The lunar controller has declared

773
00:41:40,811 --> 00:41:42,645
a state of emergency.

774
00:41:42,645 --> 00:41:45,300
Lunarville Seven has been evacuated.

775
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:47,141
All except class three instructions

776
00:41:47,141 --> 00:41:49,540
need his authorization.

777
00:41:49,540 --> 00:41:50,373
- I see.

778
00:41:51,250 --> 00:41:53,590
I'll ask for his permission when he wakes.

779
00:41:53,590 --> 00:41:55,730
- [SID] This would be important.

780
00:41:55,730 --> 00:41:57,703
Good rest Captain Scarlet.

781
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:00,473
- Goodnight, SID.

782
00:42:02,827 --> 00:42:03,660
- [Servo] Goodnight, SID.

783
00:42:03,660 --> 00:42:04,883
- [Joel] Goodnight, SID.

784
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:07,993
- [Crow] Who's SID?

785
00:42:07,993 --> 00:42:09,063
- Captain Blue, wake up.

786
00:42:10,062 --> 00:42:10,895
- What is it?

787
00:42:10,895 --> 00:42:13,540
- The lunar controller
has declared an emergency.

788
00:42:13,540 --> 00:42:16,000
Lunarville Seven has been evacuated.

789
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,960
- [Joel] Nice PJs Captain Blue.

790
00:42:17,960 --> 00:42:19,530
- If only we had a Mysteron detector,

791
00:42:19,530 --> 00:42:20,530
we could be sure.

792
00:42:20,530 --> 00:42:21,980
- Yes, but we never
would have been allowed

793
00:42:21,980 --> 00:42:23,520
to land with one.

794
00:42:23,520 --> 00:42:24,430
- Well, what do you suggest?

795
00:42:24,430 --> 00:42:25,750
- We must get a moon mobile

796
00:42:25,750 --> 00:42:27,530
and check out the Humbalt Sea.

797
00:42:27,530 --> 00:42:29,010
The answer may be there.

798
00:42:29,010 --> 00:42:30,690
- Easier said than done.

799
00:42:30,690 --> 00:42:32,160
- I'll take care of it.

800
00:42:32,160 --> 00:42:34,616
Wake Leftenant Green and
meet me at air lock three.

801
00:42:34,616 --> 00:42:38,116
(Leftenant Green snoring)

802
00:42:52,793 --> 00:42:55,376
(upbeat music)

803
00:43:12,808 --> 00:43:15,391
(upbeat music)

804
00:43:17,789 --> 00:43:18,963
- How'd you get Sid to let us out?

805
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:21,080
- I'll explain later.

806
00:43:21,080 --> 00:43:22,600
You think you can handle the controls?

807
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,430
- Yes, I'll manage.

808
00:43:24,430 --> 00:43:26,606
- Leftenant Green, have
you got that map reference.

809
00:43:26,606 --> 00:43:27,950
- Yes, Captain Scarlet.

810
00:43:27,950 --> 00:43:29,793
- Right, you will act as navigator.

811
00:43:29,793 --> 00:43:30,940
- Sig.

812
00:43:30,940 --> 00:43:31,773
- Let's go.

813
00:43:31,773 --> 00:43:32,873
- [Joel] He sure is bossy.

814
00:43:38,251 --> 00:43:40,751
- [Servo] Let's go to the hop.

815
00:43:56,630 --> 00:43:57,463
Thank you.

816
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:08,967
- What's our ETA as the Humbalt Sea?

817
00:44:08,967 --> 00:44:10,540
- 0400 hours.

818
00:44:10,540 --> 00:44:12,677
- Two hours. We might
just have time to get back

819
00:44:12,677 --> 00:44:15,070
before the lunar controller
discovers we're gone.

820
00:44:15,070 --> 00:44:17,020
- [Servo] He's got a pack of Marlboros.

821
00:44:22,621 --> 00:44:25,288
(Joel coughing)

822
00:44:28,493 --> 00:44:30,593
- [Servo] A hunka hunka burning moon rock.

823
00:44:44,658 --> 00:44:47,241
(ship hissing)

824
00:45:02,589 --> 00:45:04,800
- Well, we've covered the whole area

825
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:06,126
and found absolutely nothing.

826
00:45:06,126 --> 00:45:08,800
Another 10 minutes, then we'll start back.

827
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:10,660
- I thought I saw a light.

828
00:45:10,660 --> 00:45:11,640
- [Colonel] Where?

829
00:45:11,640 --> 00:45:13,360
- About two miles ahead.

830
00:45:13,360 --> 00:45:14,403
15 degrees to port.

831
00:45:20,551 --> 00:45:21,570
- [Colonel] I don't see anything.

832
00:45:21,570 --> 00:45:26,021
- Wait, but look, there it is again.

833
00:45:26,021 --> 00:45:29,013
- Yes, it's coming from a small crater.

834
00:45:30,490 --> 00:45:31,700
Must be here.

835
00:45:31,700 --> 00:45:34,610
It's marked but unnamed crater 101.

836
00:45:34,610 --> 00:45:35,616
Let's get over there and investigate.

837
00:45:35,616 --> 00:45:37,699
- [Servo] It's you, Joel.

838
00:45:44,140 --> 00:45:45,820
- What can it be?

839
00:45:45,820 --> 00:45:47,590
- From the amount of dust,

840
00:45:47,590 --> 00:45:49,567
there's a lot of activity down there.

841
00:45:49,567 --> 00:45:51,723
- We'll soon know.

842
00:45:51,723 --> 00:45:54,723
(satellite hissing)

843
00:46:04,990 --> 00:46:06,287
- Stop the moon mobile.

844
00:46:14,752 --> 00:46:18,027
- [Joel] Looks like a
giant pinball machine.

845
00:46:18,027 --> 00:46:19,510
- And those vehicles there,

846
00:46:19,510 --> 00:46:21,183
moving in such strange patterns.

847
00:46:22,060 --> 00:46:23,570
- You're the electronics
expert, Leftenant,

848
00:46:23,570 --> 00:46:25,090
what do you think?

849
00:46:25,090 --> 00:46:26,290
- They must be unmanned.

850
00:46:27,186 --> 00:46:30,173
They pattern is a complicated program.

851
00:46:30,173 --> 00:46:33,750
They've been program to
carried out a set task.

852
00:46:33,750 --> 00:46:35,600
- They seem to be doodling something.

853
00:46:37,210 --> 00:46:39,627
- [Servo] What's a leftenant?

854
00:46:42,181 --> 00:46:43,600
- There is no possible doubt,

855
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:46,670
exactly as the film from
the MEV on Mars showed it.

856
00:46:46,670 --> 00:46:47,820
- A Mysteron complex

857
00:46:47,820 --> 00:46:49,363
and it looks near completion.

858
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:51,720
We've seen enough.

859
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:53,070
We must get back to Lunarville Seven

860
00:46:53,070 --> 00:46:54,570
and report this to cloud base.

861
00:46:59,799 --> 00:47:02,549
(dramatic music)

862
00:47:05,780 --> 00:47:07,020
- [Joel] Looks like the micro brewery.

863
00:47:07,020 --> 00:47:08,040
- They can't have gone.

864
00:47:08,040 --> 00:47:09,460
- I assure you, sir.

865
00:47:09,460 --> 00:47:10,340
- When? How?

866
00:47:10,340 --> 00:47:12,520
- I don't know, I went
into their room and-

867
00:47:12,520 --> 00:47:14,630
- I'm not interested in details.

868
00:47:14,630 --> 00:47:16,230
Send out every available man.

869
00:47:16,230 --> 00:47:17,240
They must be found.

870
00:47:17,240 --> 00:47:19,500
- You ordered the evacuation
of Lunarville Seven, sir.

871
00:47:19,500 --> 00:47:20,586
Everyone's left.

872
00:47:20,586 --> 00:47:24,357
- The moon mobile has just
gone past phase there.

873
00:47:24,357 --> 00:47:27,902
Captain Scarlet, Captain
Blue and Lieutenant Green

874
00:47:27,902 --> 00:47:30,492
have entered Lunarville Seven.

875
00:47:30,492 --> 00:47:31,622
- They've come back.

876
00:47:31,622 --> 00:47:34,470
Of course, bring them here at once.

877
00:47:34,470 --> 00:47:35,320
- Yes, sir.

878
00:47:35,320 --> 00:47:38,510
- What they have seen must
never get back to earth.

879
00:47:38,510 --> 00:47:39,343
Bring them here.

880
00:47:39,343 --> 00:47:41,800
- There's no need lunar controller.

881
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:43,167
On the assumption that his first note

882
00:47:43,167 --> 00:47:46,300
will be rejected and subject
to our investigation,

883
00:47:46,300 --> 00:47:47,870
the world president authorized me

884
00:47:47,870 --> 00:47:49,650
to place you under close arrest

885
00:47:49,650 --> 00:47:51,410
and escort you back to earth.

886
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:52,513
- Arrest me?

887
00:47:53,770 --> 00:47:55,573
You are fools earthmen.

888
00:47:57,430 --> 00:47:59,960
Already a complex is being built.

889
00:47:59,960 --> 00:48:02,879
Soon the Mysteron will
come to take over the moon

890
00:48:02,879 --> 00:48:05,730
and then the earth.

891
00:48:05,730 --> 00:48:07,430
- We have seen the complex

892
00:48:07,430 --> 00:48:09,550
and it will be destroyed.

893
00:48:09,550 --> 00:48:12,415
- No, you will never leave the moon alive,

894
00:48:12,415 --> 00:48:14,390
any of you.

895
00:48:14,390 --> 00:48:15,287
- Sid.

896
00:48:15,287 --> 00:48:18,220
Prepare a lunar rocket
for immediate launch.

897
00:48:18,220 --> 00:48:20,000
We are leaving at once for the Earth.

898
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:21,919
- Don't waste your breath.

899
00:48:21,919 --> 00:48:25,151
- A lunar rocket is ready at phase three.

900
00:48:25,151 --> 00:48:29,430
- No, SID, this is the lunar controller.

901
00:48:29,430 --> 00:48:31,480
Seal all exits.

902
00:48:31,480 --> 00:48:32,313
- Come on.

903
00:48:33,172 --> 00:48:34,460
- [Crow] Er, er.

904
00:48:34,460 --> 00:48:36,596
- I am giving you an order.

905
00:48:36,596 --> 00:48:38,713
- [Servo] See it?

906
00:48:38,713 --> 00:48:41,220
Never mind.
- Let's go.

907
00:48:41,220 --> 00:48:45,082
- I command you, seal all exits.

908
00:48:45,082 --> 00:48:46,084
- [Joel] Okay, I get it.

909
00:48:46,084 --> 00:48:46,980
- It's not use good lunar controller,

910
00:48:46,980 --> 00:48:48,207
SID cannot identify you.

911
00:48:48,207 --> 00:48:49,110
- [Servo] I figured you would.

912
00:48:49,110 --> 00:48:50,884
- I changed recognition
discs with you last night.

913
00:48:50,884 --> 00:48:54,970
- SID, this is the lunar controller.

914
00:48:54,970 --> 00:48:55,970
Stop them.

915
00:48:55,970 --> 00:48:58,020
Seal all exits.

916
00:48:58,020 --> 00:49:00,655
- [SID] I'm sorry seal recognition disc

917
00:49:00,655 --> 00:49:02,319
cannot authorize that.

918
00:49:02,319 --> 00:49:03,402
- Obey, obey.

919
00:49:04,293 --> 00:49:05,540
Seal all exits.

920
00:49:05,540 --> 00:49:08,140
- [SID] I am sorry, your recognition disc

921
00:49:08,140 --> 00:49:09,633
does not authorize that.

922
00:49:11,620 --> 00:49:12,550
- Enter the air lock.

923
00:49:12,550 --> 00:49:14,210
The rocket's ready for launch.

924
00:49:14,210 --> 00:49:16,300
- This is your last chance, SID.

925
00:49:16,300 --> 00:49:18,320
Seal all exits.

926
00:49:18,320 --> 00:49:20,866
- [SID] I am sorry, your recognition disc.

927
00:49:20,866 --> 00:49:23,535
(gun fires)

928
00:49:23,535 --> 00:49:24,452
I am sorry.

929
00:49:26,084 --> 00:49:28,504
- [Joel] I hate the sight of oil.

930
00:49:28,504 --> 00:49:30,682
- Come on, let's get out of here.

931
00:49:30,682 --> 00:49:33,434
- [Servo] Makes me cringe.

932
00:49:33,434 --> 00:49:34,490
- Obey!

933
00:49:34,490 --> 00:49:36,230
(gun fires)

934
00:49:36,230 --> 00:49:37,570
- [Joel] All right, already.

935
00:49:37,570 --> 00:49:39,955
- [Crow] You know there
was an off switch, dummo.

936
00:49:39,955 --> 00:49:42,368
(Joel laughing)

937
00:49:42,368 --> 00:49:43,951
- [SID] I am sorry.

938
00:49:48,267 --> 00:49:51,373
- [Crow] I'm sorry you had to see that.

939
00:49:51,373 --> 00:49:53,569
It wasn't pretty.

940
00:49:53,569 --> 00:49:54,969
- [Servo] I'm all choked up.

941
00:49:56,116 --> 00:49:58,066
- [Joel] There goes that micro brewery.

942
00:49:59,240 --> 00:50:01,210
- [Crow] I only hope they get the writer.

943
00:50:01,210 --> 00:50:02,043
- Take off.

944
00:50:03,710 --> 00:50:06,627
(rocket exploding)

945
00:50:15,771 --> 00:50:17,623
- [Servo] There's still a
little cone in front of me.

946
00:50:20,170 --> 00:50:21,003
Yay.

947
00:50:25,920 --> 00:50:27,010
- Stop the picture.

948
00:50:28,320 --> 00:50:29,560
There's no possible doubt.

949
00:50:29,560 --> 00:50:31,893
That shot proves conclusively-
- [Joel] Looks like a bunch

950
00:50:31,893 --> 00:50:32,901
of giant martinis in the background.

951
00:50:32,901 --> 00:50:34,180
- The far side of the moon houses

952
00:50:34,180 --> 00:50:35,450
a Mysteron Complex.

953
00:50:35,450 --> 00:50:36,759
- Yes, Colonel, we were shocked-

954
00:50:36,759 --> 00:50:38,420
- [Servo] I think they're gin an tonics.

955
00:50:38,420 --> 00:50:40,930
- Must, of course, be
destroyed as soon as possible.

956
00:50:40,930 --> 00:50:42,230
- When do we leave, sir?

957
00:50:42,230 --> 00:50:44,030
- Wait, there's something else.

958
00:50:44,030 --> 00:50:45,460
Here's the plan.

959
00:50:45,460 --> 00:50:46,994
It has been decided to
divide the operation

960
00:50:46,994 --> 00:50:49,350
into two distinct assignments.

961
00:50:49,350 --> 00:50:50,830
- Two assignments, Colonel?

962
00:50:50,830 --> 00:50:51,884
- Yes, Captain Blue.

963
00:50:51,884 --> 00:50:55,180
The second is to destroy
the Mysteron complex.

964
00:50:55,180 --> 00:50:56,210
Arrangements have been made

965
00:50:56,210 --> 00:50:58,350
with the lunar authorities
to carry this out.

966
00:50:58,350 --> 00:50:59,500
- And the first?

967
00:50:59,500 --> 00:51:01,110
- The first is more dangerous.

968
00:51:01,110 --> 00:51:03,770
It involves a calculated
risk of the first magnitude.

969
00:51:03,770 --> 00:51:04,660
- [Joel] Combing your hair?

970
00:51:04,660 --> 00:51:06,466
- If we tried to destroy that complex-

971
00:51:06,466 --> 00:51:07,386
- [Servo] No, leaving his chair.

972
00:51:07,386 --> 00:51:08,440
- Presumably the Mysterons
will use their powers

973
00:51:08,440 --> 00:51:09,860
to reconstruct it.

974
00:51:09,860 --> 00:51:11,070
Therefore, it has been decided

975
00:51:11,070 --> 00:51:13,258
to send a volunteer party into crater 101

976
00:51:13,258 --> 00:51:16,150
into the Mysteron complex.

977
00:51:16,150 --> 00:51:18,189
Objective, to find and remove

978
00:51:18,189 --> 00:51:20,748
the power source from the complex.

979
00:51:20,748 --> 00:51:23,498
(dramatic music)

980
00:51:37,150 --> 00:51:39,350
Right, you've all had time to consider.

981
00:51:39,350 --> 00:51:42,550
As I said, this assignment
is on a volunteer basis.

982
00:51:42,550 --> 00:51:43,720
Your decisions can be made

983
00:51:43,720 --> 00:51:45,360
in the strictest confidence.

984
00:51:45,360 --> 00:51:46,770
- I'm ready to go, sir.

985
00:51:46,770 --> 00:51:48,040
- Thank you, Leftenant.

986
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:49,315
As the electronics expert you will play

987
00:51:49,315 --> 00:51:51,240
a vital part in the operation.

988
00:51:51,240 --> 00:51:52,410
- Count me in, sir.

989
00:51:52,410 --> 00:51:53,490
- Thank you, Captain.

990
00:51:53,490 --> 00:51:54,823
I know I can rely on you.

991
00:51:57,482 --> 00:51:59,020
- Well, Colonel, I am due

992
00:51:59,020 --> 00:52:00,834
for 48 hours furlough in Miami,

993
00:52:00,834 --> 00:52:03,054
but I couldn't really relax knowing

994
00:52:03,054 --> 00:52:04,410
the kind of trouble these two

995
00:52:04,410 --> 00:52:05,656
would get into without me.

996
00:52:05,656 --> 00:52:06,489
(Joel laughs)

997
00:52:06,489 --> 00:52:07,416
I'm ready, Colonel.

998
00:52:07,416 --> 00:52:08,249
- [Servo] Heba, heba.

999
00:52:08,249 --> 00:52:09,374
- Thank you, Captain Scarlet.

1000
00:52:09,374 --> 00:52:12,105
Well, gentlemen, no one knows who or what

1001
00:52:12,105 --> 00:52:15,040
you will find inside that complex.

1002
00:52:15,040 --> 00:52:17,182
All that remains for me
to do is to wish you luck.

1003
00:52:17,182 --> 00:52:19,932
(dramatic music)

1004
00:52:21,130 --> 00:52:22,830
- [Crow] That gives me a headache.

1005
00:52:30,632 --> 00:52:32,760
- This is a scale model of crater 101

1006
00:52:32,760 --> 00:52:35,070
and the surrounding area.

1007
00:52:35,070 --> 00:52:37,780
It was built up from
extensive aerial recognizance

1008
00:52:37,780 --> 00:52:39,333
over the past few days.

1009
00:52:39,333 --> 00:52:41,060
- What do we know about the vehicles

1010
00:52:41,060 --> 00:52:42,480
which were building the complex?

1011
00:52:42,480 --> 00:52:44,060
- They are unmanned lunar vehicles,

1012
00:52:44,060 --> 00:52:46,217
programmed to carry out the task.

1013
00:52:46,217 --> 00:52:50,230
This larger one controls the operation.

1014
00:52:50,230 --> 00:52:52,570
- We don't know how or
when all this was started.

1015
00:52:52,570 --> 00:52:55,440
- The lunar controller
was a Mysteron agent.

1016
00:52:55,440 --> 00:52:56,620
The secret died with him

1017
00:52:56,620 --> 00:52:58,530
when Lunarville Seven was destroyed.

1018
00:52:58,530 --> 00:53:00,750
- Well, the plan of attack is obvious.

1019
00:53:00,750 --> 00:53:02,080
Knock out the control vehicle,

1020
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:03,490
then tackle the complex.

1021
00:53:03,490 --> 00:53:06,760
- We have decided to use
a low yield atomic device

1022
00:53:06,760 --> 00:53:08,510
to destroy the complex after

1023
00:53:08,510 --> 00:53:10,400
you have had time to investigate it.

1024
00:53:10,400 --> 00:53:12,000
- Good. When do we leave?

1025
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:12,930
- At once.

1026
00:53:12,930 --> 00:53:14,600
You will travel by moon mobile.

1027
00:53:14,600 --> 00:53:15,433
- [Servo] Nice glasses.

1028
00:53:15,433 --> 00:53:17,538
- It will only take two hours.

1029
00:53:17,538 --> 00:53:18,539
And the arrangements-

1030
00:53:18,539 --> 00:53:20,700
- [Joel] They look like swimming goggles.

1031
00:53:20,700 --> 00:53:22,060
- Yes, Ms. Noland.

1032
00:53:22,060 --> 00:53:23,230
I will follow the moon mobile.

1033
00:53:23,230 --> 00:53:24,843
- [Servo] Can puppets swim?

1034
00:53:25,840 --> 00:53:26,911
- This will be positioned in the crater

1035
00:53:26,911 --> 00:53:29,599
and the detonator set for midnight,

1036
00:53:29,599 --> 00:53:31,045
standard earth time.

1037
00:53:31,045 --> 00:53:32,200
- Good.

1038
00:53:32,200 --> 00:53:34,680
That gives you six hours Captain Scarlet,

1039
00:53:34,680 --> 00:53:36,310
two to get to crater 101

1040
00:53:36,310 --> 00:53:38,292
and four hours to remove the power source

1041
00:53:38,292 --> 00:53:39,900
and get clear.

1042
00:53:39,900 --> 00:53:41,273
- Right, we're on our way.

1043
00:53:42,450 --> 00:53:43,460
- Captain Scarlet.

1044
00:53:43,460 --> 00:53:45,001
- Yes, Ms. Noland.

1045
00:53:45,001 --> 00:53:48,070
- I'd like you to take this.

1046
00:53:48,070 --> 00:53:49,631
It's a lucky charm.

1047
00:53:49,631 --> 00:53:53,550
I'm not really superstitious,
but please take it.

1048
00:53:53,550 --> 00:53:58,440
- To Linda Noland, the CB29 Neptune probe,

1049
00:53:58,440 --> 00:54:01,400
July 10, 2058.

1050
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:03,100
We made it ahead of schedule.

1051
00:54:03,100 --> 00:54:04,310
- I remember.

1052
00:54:04,310 --> 00:54:05,510
You were the project controller

1053
00:54:05,510 --> 00:54:07,940
on the first Neptune probe
launched from the moon.

1054
00:54:07,940 --> 00:54:09,200
- Yes, Captain Blue.

1055
00:54:09,200 --> 00:54:10,720
- [Captain Blue] Let's
home we're as successful.

1056
00:54:10,720 --> 00:54:12,360
- Be careful, Captain.

1057
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:15,150
- Don't worry, we intend to come back.

1058
00:54:15,150 --> 00:54:15,983
Let's go.

1059
00:54:15,983 --> 00:54:18,280
- [Servo] I need to go to
some radiator maintenance.

1060
00:54:18,280 --> 00:54:19,113
- A brave man.

1061
00:54:19,113 --> 00:54:21,190
And very good looking.

1062
00:54:21,190 --> 00:54:22,023
- Who?

1063
00:54:22,023 --> 00:54:22,866
- Captain Scarlet.

1064
00:54:22,866 --> 00:54:26,750
- Yes, I suppose so, I
didn't really notice.

1065
00:54:26,750 --> 00:54:28,150
- Yes, Ms. Noland.

1066
00:54:29,627 --> 00:54:32,294
(ominous music)

1067
00:54:37,457 --> 00:54:40,624
(moon mobile hissing)

1068
00:54:47,611 --> 00:54:50,028
- ETA crater 101, 55 minutes.

1069
00:54:59,366 --> 00:55:02,533
(moon mobile hissing)

1070
00:55:11,470 --> 00:55:13,350
- It's time for you to leave, Frazier.

1071
00:55:13,350 --> 00:55:14,490
- Yes, Ms. Noland.

1072
00:55:14,490 --> 00:55:17,827
- Remember, set the
detonator for midnight SET.

1073
00:55:18,780 --> 00:55:20,580
We must give them time to get clear.

1074
00:55:23,220 --> 00:55:24,053
Frazier?

1075
00:55:25,200 --> 00:55:26,980
Frazier, are you all right?

1076
00:55:26,980 --> 00:55:28,660
- Yes, I'm fine.

1077
00:55:28,660 --> 00:55:31,089
Your instructions will be carried out.

1078
00:55:31,089 --> 00:55:33,839
(dramatic music)

1079
00:55:36,674 --> 00:55:39,257
(upbeat music)

1080
00:55:45,019 --> 00:55:47,602
(upbeat music)

1081
00:55:50,000 --> 00:55:51,480
- If the turkey comes out of his hole

1082
00:55:51,480 --> 00:55:54,788
and sees his shadow,
that means we have six

1083
00:55:54,788 --> 00:55:57,115
more weeks of Easter?

1084
00:55:57,115 --> 00:55:58,810
- No, Crow, it's not like this.

1085
00:55:58,810 --> 00:56:00,294
Back at my house when I was on Earth,

1086
00:56:00,294 --> 00:56:04,620
we would have Thanksgiving
dinner around 2 o'clock,

1087
00:56:04,620 --> 00:56:07,400
have mashed potatoes, turkey, yams,

1088
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:08,810
the whole shebang.

1089
00:56:08,810 --> 00:56:10,598
Then around dinner time,

1090
00:56:10,598 --> 00:56:13,530
around six or seven, we'd
have turkey sandwiches

1091
00:56:13,530 --> 00:56:15,320
even if we weren't hungry.

1092
00:56:15,320 --> 00:56:17,851
Then later that night my
mom would cut up the turkey

1093
00:56:17,851 --> 00:56:21,290
some more and put it in
Tupperware for the drive home.

1094
00:56:21,290 --> 00:56:24,780
- And for breakfast turkey crisp cereal?

1095
00:56:24,780 --> 00:56:26,321
- Right.

1096
00:56:26,321 --> 00:56:27,341
- I'm right?

1097
00:56:27,341 --> 00:56:29,670
You see that time I
was trying to be funny.

1098
00:56:29,670 --> 00:56:31,690
I'm never going to catch on.

1099
00:56:31,690 --> 00:56:32,680
- Crow, I was just kidding,

1100
00:56:32,680 --> 00:56:33,730
I was just getting into it,

1101
00:56:33,730 --> 00:56:36,847
like I would say
cocoa-flavored Thanksgiving,

1102
00:56:36,847 --> 00:56:37,680
you get it?

1103
00:56:37,680 --> 00:56:39,931
- (laughs) Oh, very funny Joel Hodgson.

1104
00:56:39,931 --> 00:56:42,850
Don't forget Kellogg's beaks and feet.

1105
00:56:42,850 --> 00:56:45,150
- Right, or raisins, rice and giblets.

1106
00:56:45,150 --> 00:56:46,340
Hi, Servo.

1107
00:56:46,340 --> 00:56:48,430
(talking over each other)

1108
00:56:48,430 --> 00:56:49,263
Great.

1109
00:56:49,263 --> 00:56:52,982
- Hmm, let's see, things
that are in a mattress.

1110
00:56:52,982 --> 00:56:55,626
Things that have somebody for dessert.

1111
00:56:55,626 --> 00:56:58,500
Things that Dick Clark
might say in his sleep.

1112
00:56:58,500 --> 00:57:00,030
- No, toasted turkey trots Servo.

1113
00:57:00,030 --> 00:57:02,113
- Things you might say on a TV show

1114
00:57:02,113 --> 00:57:03,606
if you were trying to take up time.

1115
00:57:03,606 --> 00:57:04,780
- Moto turkey.

1116
00:57:04,780 --> 00:57:06,270
- Things you might eat for breakfast

1117
00:57:06,270 --> 00:57:08,020
the day after Thanksgiving
if you were just kidding.

1118
00:57:08,020 --> 00:57:09,511
- Right, you got it.

1119
00:57:09,511 --> 00:57:12,609
Oh, we got movie siren,
guys, we gotta get out here.

1120
00:57:12,609 --> 00:57:13,442
Cheese it.

1121
00:57:18,498 --> 00:57:21,248
(doors clanking)

1122
00:57:22,450 --> 00:57:24,060
- I am aboard the lunar tank

1123
00:57:24,060 --> 00:57:25,430
and ready to leave.

1124
00:57:25,430 --> 00:57:26,530
- Right.

1125
00:57:26,530 --> 00:57:28,550
Report in an hour, Frazier.

1126
00:57:28,550 --> 00:57:30,881
We're tracking okay now.

1127
00:57:30,881 --> 00:57:33,548
(tank whirring)

1128
00:57:48,779 --> 00:57:50,362
- [Joel] Hey, Crow.

1129
00:57:51,265 --> 00:57:52,182
Hey, Servo.

1130
00:57:53,142 --> 00:57:54,309
Hmm, he's big.

1131
00:57:58,347 --> 00:58:00,097
- [Crow] He could use a Q-tip, too.

1132
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:02,960
- I have Captain Scarlet

1133
00:58:02,960 --> 00:58:04,830
on the inner space radio link, sir.

1134
00:58:04,830 --> 00:58:06,230
- Good, let me speak to him.

1135
00:58:08,520 --> 00:58:09,400
Captain Scarlet?

1136
00:58:09,400 --> 00:58:10,401
- Yes, Colonel.

1137
00:58:10,401 --> 00:58:12,800
We're about the cross the lunar horizon.

1138
00:58:12,800 --> 00:58:14,637
We will then be on the far
side of the moon from earth

1139
00:58:14,637 --> 00:58:16,203
and we lose all radio contact.

1140
00:58:16,203 --> 00:58:17,180
- I understand, Captain.

1141
00:58:17,180 --> 00:58:19,164
What's the latest situation?

1142
00:58:19,164 --> 00:58:20,630
- When we arrive at the crater,

1143
00:58:20,630 --> 00:58:22,247
we will immobilize the control vehicle

1144
00:58:22,247 --> 00:58:23,776
and then enter the complex.

1145
00:58:23,776 --> 00:58:25,320
After our investigation,

1146
00:58:25,320 --> 00:58:27,103
the whole area will be
destroyed at midnight

1147
00:58:27,103 --> 00:58:28,710
standard earth time.

1148
00:58:28,710 --> 00:58:30,670
- SIG, Captain.

1149
00:58:30,670 --> 00:58:32,993
Report back as soon as the
radio link is restored.

1150
00:58:32,993 --> 00:58:34,235
- [Servo] What's SIG?

1151
00:58:34,235 --> 00:58:35,901
- Sig.
- What are the chances, sir?

1152
00:58:35,901 --> 00:58:38,390
- [Joel] He gets a cigarette
if he does it right.

1153
00:58:38,390 --> 00:58:41,010
- Men have faced the unknown before,

1154
00:58:41,010 --> 00:58:42,340
but I believe no man has ever faced

1155
00:58:42,340 --> 00:58:44,363
what awaits them in crater 101.

1156
00:58:46,267 --> 00:58:47,377
- [Servo] Carol Mastro.

1157
00:58:47,377 --> 00:58:48,993
- [Joel] Carol Marrow.

1158
00:58:50,924 --> 00:58:52,947
Crater number one.

1159
00:58:55,782 --> 00:58:57,615
- [Crow] Take the box.

1160
00:59:03,213 --> 00:59:04,849
- It's just over this ridge.

1161
00:59:04,849 --> 00:59:05,682
- Sig.

1162
00:59:06,545 --> 00:59:09,212
(ominous music)

1163
00:59:16,940 --> 00:59:18,438
- Stop the moon mobile.

1164
00:59:18,438 --> 00:59:19,271
Look.

1165
00:59:21,173 --> 00:59:22,823
- [Crow] It's a Tupperware party.

1166
00:59:27,248 --> 00:59:29,570
- [Joel] A giant vacuum cleaner.

1167
00:59:29,570 --> 00:59:30,970
- [Crow] That puts out dust.

1168
00:59:34,531 --> 00:59:37,960
- Well, it answers one
question, how to get in.

1169
00:59:37,960 --> 00:59:40,350
- You mean, we are going the same way?

1170
00:59:40,350 --> 00:59:41,840
- Yes, Leftenant.

1171
00:59:41,840 --> 00:59:42,880
Let's get into the moon tractor.

1172
00:59:42,880 --> 00:59:44,803
- [Joel] Disguised as dust balls.

1173
00:59:49,190 --> 00:59:50,210
- [Servo] I found being a dust bunny

1174
00:59:50,210 --> 00:59:55,210
can get you into a lot of places.

1175
00:59:58,617 --> 01:00:00,793
- [Crow] I can see the string.

1176
01:00:05,190 --> 01:00:09,023
- We've got to knock out
that control vehicle.

1177
01:00:10,886 --> 01:00:11,729
- They're going to attack.

1178
01:00:11,729 --> 01:00:12,859
- [Servo] Scrubbing bubbles.

1179
01:00:12,859 --> 01:00:16,721
- Lieutenant Green, man the missile gun.

1180
01:00:16,721 --> 01:00:18,936
Look out, Captain Blue.

1181
01:00:18,936 --> 01:00:23,186
- [Crow] I hate to see what
they'd do to a bathtub.

1182
01:00:25,540 --> 01:00:26,840
- There's another, swerve.

1183
01:00:30,289 --> 01:00:32,175
- [Servo] Zig.

1184
01:00:32,175 --> 01:00:34,580
- Can you see the control vehicle?

1185
01:00:34,580 --> 01:00:36,200
- There's so much dust.

1186
01:00:36,200 --> 01:00:37,983
- There it is, dead ahead.

1187
01:00:41,570 --> 01:00:42,403
- Fire.

1188
01:00:44,891 --> 01:00:46,490
- Missed.

1189
01:00:46,490 --> 01:00:51,053
Don't lose sight of it.

1190
01:01:00,619 --> 01:01:01,452
Stop!

1191
01:01:03,883 --> 01:01:06,710
(machine crashes)

1192
01:01:06,710 --> 01:01:08,879
- [Servo] It's like a tractor
pull kind of. (Joel laughs)

1193
01:01:08,879 --> 01:01:10,050
- [Servo] They'll turn the moon

1194
01:01:10,050 --> 01:01:12,020
into a giant mud pit.

1195
01:01:12,020 --> 01:01:12,853
- We're stuck.

1196
01:01:14,900 --> 01:01:16,900
- [Captain Blue] Look, it's coming back.

1197
01:01:24,450 --> 01:01:25,583
- Keep trying.

1198
01:01:28,850 --> 01:01:30,651
- It's no good, it won't budge.

1199
01:01:30,651 --> 01:01:32,180
- It'll smash us to pieces.

1200
01:01:32,180 --> 01:01:34,811
- There's the control vehicle.

1201
01:01:34,811 --> 01:01:36,590
- [Joel] You want some popcorn?

1202
01:01:36,590 --> 01:01:37,560
- [Crow] Yes, please.

1203
01:01:37,560 --> 01:01:40,533
- You have one chance left,
Leftenant, don't miss.

1204
01:01:46,000 --> 01:01:48,333
(gun fires)

1205
01:01:50,715 --> 01:01:53,632
(machines hissing)

1206
01:01:54,530 --> 01:01:55,710
- Do I get a coconut?

1207
01:01:55,710 --> 01:01:57,124
- If we ever get out of this Leftenant,

1208
01:01:57,124 --> 01:01:59,637
I'll buy you all the coconuts you can eat.

1209
01:02:02,342 --> 01:02:05,120
- Lunarville Six to lunar tank,

1210
01:02:05,120 --> 01:02:06,633
what is your position?

1211
01:02:06,633 --> 01:02:09,660
- I am about to cross the lunar horizon.

1212
01:02:09,660 --> 01:02:10,630
- Right.

1213
01:02:10,630 --> 01:02:13,857
Remember, set the detonator
for 12 o'clock SET.

1214
01:02:14,970 --> 01:02:17,243
- I am sorry, earth woman.

1215
01:02:17,243 --> 01:02:18,810
- Earth woman?

1216
01:02:18,810 --> 01:02:22,573
- The detonator is already set for 10,

1217
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:26,980
two hours earlier than Spectrum think.

1218
01:02:26,980 --> 01:02:29,470
- Frazier, listen to me Frazier.

1219
01:02:29,470 --> 01:02:30,864
- Captain Scarlet is below

1220
01:02:30,864 --> 01:02:33,450
the lunar horizon.

1221
01:02:33,450 --> 01:02:35,283
You cannot contact him.

1222
01:02:36,440 --> 01:02:39,467
He will die in crater 101.

1223
01:02:42,992 --> 01:02:44,813
- Lieutenant Green's
freed the lunar tractor.

1224
01:02:44,813 --> 01:02:46,160
We're ready to go.

1225
01:02:46,160 --> 01:02:46,993
- Good.

1226
01:02:46,993 --> 01:02:50,768
And there's Frazier in the
atomic device right on time.

1227
01:02:50,768 --> 01:02:53,518
(dramatic music)

1228
01:02:56,450 --> 01:02:58,203
Tell Lieutenant Green to get back in here.

1229
01:02:58,203 --> 01:02:59,036
- Sig.

1230
01:03:03,760 --> 01:03:06,730
- Captain Scarlet to lunar
tank, come in Frazier.

1231
01:03:06,730 --> 01:03:08,730
- I'm about to release the atomic device.

1232
01:03:08,730 --> 01:03:11,362
- [Captain Scarlet] Right,
we'll start the investigation.

1233
01:03:11,362 --> 01:03:12,406
- Good luck.

1234
01:03:12,406 --> 01:03:14,880
- [Joel] I'm gonna put the rest
of the popcorn in your head.

1235
01:03:14,880 --> 01:03:16,610
- Goodbye earth man.

1236
01:03:16,610 --> 01:03:18,373
- [Servo] I was hoping you'd say that.

1237
01:03:28,193 --> 01:03:30,943
- [Joel] We'll save it for later.

1238
01:03:32,562 --> 01:03:35,312
(dramatic music)

1239
01:04:03,755 --> 01:04:07,047
- [Servo] Traction,
traction, action, action.

1240
01:04:07,047 --> 01:04:08,653
- [Joel] Power, power, power.

1241
01:04:18,774 --> 01:04:20,320
- [Crow] I bet they're all tankful

1242
01:04:20,320 --> 01:04:21,370
they got out of that.

1243
01:04:23,115 --> 01:04:24,321
- [Joel] Good one, Crow.

1244
01:04:24,321 --> 01:04:25,571
- [Crow] Sorry.

1245
01:04:29,240 --> 01:04:33,160
- [Colonel] Radio check,
Captain Blue, spectrum is green.

1246
01:04:33,160 --> 01:04:33,993
Leftenant, radio is-

1247
01:04:33,993 --> 01:04:35,800
- [Servo] Care for a
stove full of popcorn.

1248
01:04:35,800 --> 01:04:36,678
- [Colonel] Let's go in.

1249
01:04:36,678 --> 01:04:38,187
- [Captain Blue] Through the wall?

1250
01:04:38,187 --> 01:04:39,637
- [Colonel] Through the wall.

1251
01:04:41,430 --> 01:04:42,930
- [Joel] It won't come around.

1252
01:04:49,920 --> 01:04:51,760
- It's indescribable.

1253
01:04:51,760 --> 01:04:54,113
- Start the cameras, let's move on.

1254
01:04:56,200 --> 01:04:58,750
- [Joel] Those Mysterons
sure know how to decorate.

1255
01:05:00,971 --> 01:05:01,870
- [Crow] Psychedelic.

1256
01:05:01,870 --> 01:05:03,970
- [Joel] Kind of like Peter Max was there.

1257
01:05:05,537 --> 01:05:06,419
- [Servo] Purple haze all in my brain.

1258
01:05:06,419 --> 01:05:07,510
- [Colonel] Take it easy, Leftenant,

1259
01:05:07,510 --> 01:05:08,737
you're forgetting the low gravity.

1260
01:05:08,737 --> 01:05:09,863
- Sig.

1261
01:05:13,050 --> 01:05:14,630
- There's no radiation.

1262
01:05:14,630 --> 01:05:15,640
What's the temperature?

1263
01:05:15,640 --> 01:05:16,990
- Normal.

1264
01:05:16,990 --> 01:05:20,693
Gravity and pressure fluctuation negative.

1265
01:05:23,010 --> 01:05:23,843
- [Servo] No pressure fluctuation.

1266
01:05:23,843 --> 01:05:26,779
- No trace of any x-ray
or infrared emission?

1267
01:05:26,779 --> 01:05:28,303
- No, nothing so far.

1268
01:05:29,170 --> 01:05:31,240
Where's Leftenant Green?

1269
01:05:31,240 --> 01:05:32,573
Leftenant Green?

1270
01:05:33,740 --> 01:05:34,573
Leftenant Green?

1271
01:05:37,410 --> 01:05:38,510
- [Joel] They got him.

1272
01:05:40,600 --> 01:05:41,810
He's a Mysteron.

1273
01:05:48,620 --> 01:05:49,453
- Over there.

1274
01:05:56,840 --> 01:05:59,030
- Leftenant Green, what's wrong?

1275
01:05:59,030 --> 01:05:59,913
- [Joel] That was assy.

1276
01:05:59,913 --> 01:06:01,330
- [Servo] I know.

1277
01:06:17,330 --> 01:06:19,003
- [Servo] Joel, make a bunny shadow.

1278
01:06:22,995 --> 01:06:26,020
(gun fires)

1279
01:06:26,020 --> 01:06:29,353
- [Servo] He doesn't like bunny shadows.

1280
01:06:36,033 --> 01:06:37,540
- Another few seconds

1281
01:06:37,540 --> 01:06:39,930
and we would have all been transfixed.

1282
01:06:39,930 --> 01:06:41,560
- I couldn't look away.

1283
01:06:41,560 --> 01:06:44,330
I tried, but I just couldn't.

1284
01:06:44,330 --> 01:06:47,656
- Let's move in and stay together.

1285
01:06:47,656 --> 01:06:48,823
- [Joel] Good.

1286
01:06:51,752 --> 01:06:53,700
- Frazier is a Mysteron?

1287
01:06:53,700 --> 01:06:55,380
- Are you sure Contrilla?

1288
01:06:55,380 --> 01:06:57,190
- He told me as much himself.

1289
01:06:57,190 --> 01:07:00,520
He set the detonator for
10 o'clock instead of 12.

1290
01:07:00,520 --> 01:07:01,521
- What?

1291
01:07:01,521 --> 01:07:03,932
Isn't there some way we
can warn Captain Scarlet?

1292
01:07:03,932 --> 01:07:06,163
- No, he's out of radio range.

1293
01:07:08,710 --> 01:07:10,700
- [Joel] Radio range?
Isn't that a kind of stove.

1294
01:07:10,700 --> 01:07:12,320
- Stay back.

1295
01:07:12,320 --> 01:07:13,300
- [Captain Blue] What is it, Captain?

1296
01:07:13,300 --> 01:07:15,400
- Some kind of weightless area just

1297
01:07:15,400 --> 01:07:16,930
in front of where you're standing.

1298
01:07:16,930 --> 01:07:19,193
- [Servo] He's going up
to the Jetsons' apartment.

1299
01:07:21,310 --> 01:07:22,143
- [Crow] Astro dog like.

1300
01:07:22,143 --> 01:07:24,403
- Captain Scarlet, can you hear me?

1301
01:07:25,290 --> 01:07:28,590
- Yes, it's all right, you can come up.

1302
01:07:28,590 --> 01:07:31,983
I think I've found the
heart of the complex.

1303
01:07:37,850 --> 01:07:39,480
- [Joel] Sure helps you float when you've

1304
01:07:39,480 --> 01:07:40,907
got threads on you.

1305
01:07:41,770 --> 01:07:42,612
- Through there.

1306
01:07:42,612 --> 01:07:43,445
- [Crow] That's right.

1307
01:07:43,445 --> 01:07:44,278
- Look.

1308
01:07:46,341 --> 01:07:47,203
What is it?

1309
01:07:47,203 --> 01:07:49,740
- There's only one way to find out.

1310
01:07:49,740 --> 01:07:50,640
- [Joel] Shoot it.

1311
01:07:54,232 --> 01:07:57,149
(mysterious music)

1312
01:08:01,340 --> 01:08:04,090
- [Crow] Be careful, it's
the worst special effect yet.

1313
01:08:10,513 --> 01:08:13,414
- [Servo] This could be trouble.

1314
01:08:13,414 --> 01:08:16,700
- [Crow] Place your bets, place your bets.

1315
01:08:16,700 --> 01:08:19,110
- [Joel] They're trying to
legalize gambling on the moon.

1316
01:08:19,110 --> 01:08:21,103
- My instrumentation's gone crazy.

1317
01:08:22,310 --> 01:08:23,320
- [Joel] It's a lottery.

1318
01:08:23,320 --> 01:08:25,490
- The power source.

1319
01:08:25,490 --> 01:08:27,070
- Get as many pictures as you can.

1320
01:08:27,070 --> 01:08:28,397
We've got to work fast.

1321
01:08:28,397 --> 01:08:31,210
Remember the 12 o'clock deadline.

1322
01:08:31,210 --> 01:08:32,474
- Well, a rocket's the
only thing fast enough

1323
01:08:32,474 --> 01:08:35,762
to get there before that bomb explodes.

1324
01:08:35,762 --> 01:08:37,463
- An unmanned rocket.

1325
01:08:38,310 --> 01:08:39,250
Could it work?

1326
01:08:40,600 --> 01:08:44,170
There's the slimmest chance,
but it's the only one.

1327
01:08:44,170 --> 01:08:45,840
- Right, we've got enough pictures.

1328
01:08:45,840 --> 01:08:47,070
What time is it?

1329
01:08:47,070 --> 01:08:49,210
- 9:32 set.

1330
01:08:49,210 --> 01:08:50,380
- Good.

1331
01:08:50,380 --> 01:08:51,954
Two and a half hours to detonation,

1332
01:08:51,954 --> 01:08:53,210
we have plenty of time.

1333
01:08:53,210 --> 01:08:54,578
- [Servo] Funny how two and a half hours

1334
01:08:54,578 --> 01:08:56,411
seems like 30 minutes.

1335
01:08:57,479 --> 01:08:59,600
- The rocket is ready on the launch pad.

1336
01:08:59,600 --> 01:09:01,682
- Start the countdown immediately.

1337
01:09:01,682 --> 01:09:03,332
- [Crow] Good, another countdown.

1338
01:09:04,920 --> 01:09:07,550
- All we can do now is hope.

1339
01:09:07,550 --> 01:09:09,530
- [Servo] Well, you sure can't fart.

1340
01:09:09,530 --> 01:09:13,263
- Four, three, two, one, lift off.

1341
01:09:16,229 --> 01:09:19,146
(rocket exploding)

1342
01:09:27,685 --> 01:09:29,810
- [Crow] Got carried away.

1343
01:09:29,810 --> 01:09:33,160
- I'm going to try and
remove the power source.

1344
01:09:33,160 --> 01:09:34,360
- Take it easy, Captain.

1345
01:09:37,019 --> 01:09:39,852
(rocket whirring)

1346
01:09:50,870 --> 01:09:52,100
- What was that?

1347
01:09:52,100 --> 01:09:53,963
- I don't know. I'll go and find out.

1348
01:09:55,790 --> 01:09:58,540
- [Servo] I could sure use
a good commercial right now.

1349
01:09:59,952 --> 01:10:02,702
(dramatic music)

1350
01:10:03,941 --> 01:10:06,524
(upbeat music)

1351
01:10:24,290 --> 01:10:26,873
(upbeat music)

1352
01:10:31,340 --> 01:10:32,820
- [Colonel] Can you see
anything Captain Blue?

1353
01:10:32,820 --> 01:10:33,653
- Yes.

1354
01:10:33,653 --> 01:10:35,440
It's an unmanned space probe.

1355
01:10:35,440 --> 01:10:37,590
And old CB29.

1356
01:10:37,590 --> 01:10:39,670
It must have been launched
from Lunarville Six.

1357
01:10:39,670 --> 01:10:42,193
- But why an obsolete CB29?

1358
01:10:43,580 --> 01:10:44,820
Unless...

1359
01:10:44,820 --> 01:10:46,940
- Maybe it's some kind of message.

1360
01:10:46,940 --> 01:10:47,896
- Or a warning?

1361
01:10:47,896 --> 01:10:49,908
- Nah.
- The lucky charm.

1362
01:10:49,908 --> 01:10:51,075
- What was it?

1363
01:10:52,610 --> 01:10:56,404
To Linda Noland, the CB29 Neptune probe

1364
01:10:56,404 --> 01:10:59,620
July 10, 2058.

1365
01:10:59,620 --> 01:11:02,193
- We made it ahead of schedule.

1366
01:11:03,880 --> 01:11:05,161
Can you see a connection?

1367
01:11:05,161 --> 01:11:06,164
- [Servo] That schedule.

1368
01:11:06,164 --> 01:11:08,425
- Ahead of schedule.

1369
01:11:08,425 --> 01:11:09,258
- [Joel] Schedule!

1370
01:11:09,258 --> 01:11:10,675
- 12 o'clock SET.

1371
01:11:11,610 --> 01:11:13,240
The bomb.

1372
01:11:13,240 --> 01:11:14,978
It could mean the bomb will
explode ahead of schedule.

1373
01:11:14,978 --> 01:11:16,630
- [Servo] You just said it Leftenant.

1374
01:11:16,630 --> 01:11:18,423
- Captain Blue, check the detonator time

1375
01:11:18,423 --> 01:11:20,085
on that atomic device.

1376
01:11:20,085 --> 01:11:20,960
- [Captain Blue] SIG.

1377
01:11:20,960 --> 01:11:22,317
- Leftenant Green, get
back in the moon mobile.

1378
01:11:22,317 --> 01:11:23,260
- But Captain.

1379
01:11:23,260 --> 01:11:24,093
- That's an order.

1380
01:11:24,093 --> 01:11:26,728
- [Crow] Dano, check out every
license number on the planet.

1381
01:11:26,728 --> 01:11:27,795
- Get moving.

1382
01:11:27,795 --> 01:11:28,628
- Sig.

1383
01:11:31,078 --> 01:11:32,317
- [Joel] SIG.

1384
01:11:32,317 --> 01:11:35,716
- [Crow] I think it's a
Johnny Quest thing, SIG.

1385
01:11:35,716 --> 01:11:37,633
- [Joel] Oh, that's it.

1386
01:11:43,010 --> 01:11:46,090
- Captain Scarlet, the
detonator is set for 10.

1387
01:11:46,090 --> 01:11:47,270
Get out of there.

1388
01:11:47,270 --> 01:11:49,590
The whole crater will
go up in five minutes.

1389
01:11:49,590 --> 01:11:51,580
- Get into the moon mobile.
I'll follow as soon as I can.

1390
01:11:51,580 --> 01:11:52,448
- [Servo] How can a crater go up?

1391
01:11:52,448 --> 01:11:53,281
- I'm coming back.

1392
01:11:53,281 --> 01:11:54,950
- No, at least get the cameras to safety.

1393
01:11:54,950 --> 01:11:56,090
- [Captain Blue] Captain Scarlet.

1394
01:11:56,090 --> 01:11:59,520
- You know I'm right, Adam, do as I say.

1395
01:11:59,520 --> 01:12:00,603
- Spectrum is green.

1396
01:12:02,330 --> 01:12:04,093
- [Crow] That would just make it level.

1397
01:12:06,153 --> 01:12:08,820
(ominous music)

1398
01:12:26,345 --> 01:12:29,512
- Less than two minutes to detonation.

1399
01:12:33,710 --> 01:12:34,760
- [Joel] Just pretend you're using

1400
01:12:34,760 --> 01:12:36,660
one of those cranes at the state fair.

1401
01:12:50,590 --> 01:12:52,020
- We're safe here.

1402
01:12:52,020 --> 01:12:53,510
Any sign of Captain Scarlet?

1403
01:12:53,510 --> 01:12:54,413
- No, nothing.

1404
01:12:55,841 --> 01:12:58,591
(dramatic music)

1405
01:13:06,628 --> 01:13:09,545
(crater exploding)

1406
01:13:14,580 --> 01:13:15,700
- [Servo] The crater.

1407
01:13:15,700 --> 01:13:16,533
- [Crow] It went up.

1408
01:13:16,533 --> 01:13:17,483
- He didn't make it.

1409
01:13:18,370 --> 01:13:20,253
He just didn't make it.

1410
01:13:22,840 --> 01:13:23,673
- Look.

1411
01:13:25,871 --> 01:13:27,050
- [Man] What a guy.

1412
01:13:27,050 --> 01:13:28,950
- [Servo] I tended to doubt it myself.

1413
01:13:41,274 --> 01:13:43,300
- Well, gentlemen, I'm glad to be able

1414
01:13:43,300 --> 01:13:45,910
to tell you mission accomplished.

1415
01:13:45,910 --> 01:13:48,720
- Our recognizance shows
it was a complete success.

1416
01:13:48,720 --> 01:13:50,560
- That's great news.

1417
01:13:50,560 --> 01:13:53,020
It means that the Mysteron
powers of reconstruction

1418
01:13:53,020 --> 01:13:55,162
of somehow connected
with this power source.

1419
01:13:55,162 --> 01:13:57,550
We must take it back to earth at once.

1420
01:13:57,550 --> 01:14:00,173
Well, I'm afraid it's goodbye.

1421
01:14:02,090 --> 01:14:03,020
Thank you for everything.

1422
01:14:03,020 --> 01:14:03,877
- [Crow] No, I'm afraid it's a diamond.

1423
01:14:03,877 --> 01:14:05,620
- Goodbye, Captain Scarlet.

1424
01:14:05,620 --> 01:14:08,940
- I almost forgot, your lucky charm.

1425
01:14:08,940 --> 01:14:11,820
- I'd take it as a favor if you'd keep it.

1426
01:14:11,820 --> 01:14:12,723
- Thank you.

1427
01:14:12,723 --> 01:14:14,738
Let's go Adam.
- I think she likes him.

1428
01:14:14,738 --> 01:14:16,770
(gentle music)

1429
01:14:16,770 --> 01:14:18,090
- [Servo] Too bad she lives on the moon.

1430
01:14:18,090 --> 01:14:21,860
- A brave man and so good looking.

1431
01:14:21,860 --> 01:14:23,684
- I suppose so.

1432
01:14:23,684 --> 01:14:25,608
I didn't think you'd notice.

1433
01:14:25,608 --> 01:14:28,191
(upbeat music)

1434
01:14:35,000 --> 01:14:36,470
- I'm going down to the lounge.

1435
01:14:36,470 --> 01:14:37,896
Let me know when Captain
Scarlet makes contact

1436
01:14:37,896 --> 01:14:39,920
with Dr. Kernitz.

1437
01:14:39,920 --> 01:14:42,226
And launch Angel One to escort
them back to cloud base.

1438
01:14:42,226 --> 01:14:43,421
- Yes, Colonel.

1439
01:14:43,421 --> 01:14:46,338
(triumphant music)

1440
01:14:49,650 --> 01:14:51,784
- [Man] Angel One, immediate launch.

1441
01:14:51,784 --> 01:14:53,512
- Sig.

1442
01:14:53,512 --> 01:14:56,179
(plane soaring)

1443
01:14:58,460 --> 01:15:00,520
- Receipt of grid reference G17

1444
01:15:00,520 --> 01:15:04,810
on away to arrival of Captain
Scarlet and Dr. Kernitz.

1445
01:15:04,810 --> 01:15:07,340
- You will escort them back to cloud base.

1446
01:15:07,340 --> 01:15:10,426
This is a maximum security operation.

1447
01:15:10,426 --> 01:15:12,550
- SIG, Lieutenant Green.

1448
01:15:12,550 --> 01:15:14,317
I shall take good care of them.

1449
01:15:14,317 --> 01:15:16,653
I know how important this mission is.

1450
01:15:18,295 --> 01:15:20,878
- [Joel] Sounds like she knows.

1451
01:15:22,320 --> 01:15:23,433
Nice stereo.

1452
01:15:24,378 --> 01:15:26,760
(Servo coughing)

1453
01:15:26,760 --> 01:15:27,953
You okay?
- Popcorn.

1454
01:15:33,460 --> 01:15:34,343
- [Joel] The T94.

1455
01:15:35,690 --> 01:15:37,053
Compact disc.

1456
01:15:40,035 --> 01:15:42,785
(dramatic music)

1457
01:15:45,349 --> 01:15:48,266
(triumphant music)

1458
01:15:53,261 --> 01:15:54,373
- Leftenant Green, I'm outside

1459
01:15:54,373 --> 01:15:57,146
the Nash Institute of Technology.

1460
01:15:57,146 --> 01:15:58,234
- The helicopter reports

1461
01:15:58,234 --> 01:15:59,293
you were not followed.

1462
01:15:59,293 --> 01:16:00,987
Proceed Captain Scarlet.

1463
01:16:00,987 --> 01:16:02,501
Dr. Kernitz is expecting you.

1464
01:16:02,501 --> 01:16:03,613
- Sig.

1465
01:16:13,872 --> 01:16:16,657
(Servo squeaking)

1466
01:16:16,657 --> 01:16:17,670
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

1467
01:16:17,670 --> 01:16:20,500
- [Woman] Captain Scarlet
has arrived, Dr. Kernitz.

1468
01:16:20,500 --> 01:16:22,070
- [Dr. Kernitz] Good, tell
the Captain I am ready

1469
01:16:22,070 --> 01:16:23,120
to leave immediately.

1470
01:16:24,150 --> 01:16:26,020
- The doctor will be with
you in a minute, sir.

1471
01:16:26,020 --> 01:16:27,910
He says he's ready to leave at once.

1472
01:16:27,910 --> 01:16:29,063
- Good, thank you.

1473
01:16:30,020 --> 01:16:31,680
Captain Scarlet to Yellow Fox.

1474
01:16:31,680 --> 01:16:34,140
Proceed to rear entrance
of research center.

1475
01:16:34,140 --> 01:16:35,193
- Spectrum is green.

1476
01:16:36,086 --> 01:16:39,503
(vehicle engine revving)

1477
01:16:43,740 --> 01:16:44,750
- Ready doctor?

1478
01:16:44,750 --> 01:16:46,817
- Ready.
- You have everything?

1479
01:16:46,817 --> 01:16:47,926
- Yes.

1480
01:16:47,926 --> 01:16:50,676
(dramatic music)

1481
01:17:19,563 --> 01:17:21,036
A gasoline tanker?

1482
01:17:21,036 --> 01:17:23,033
- I think you'll find it comfortable.

1483
01:17:27,920 --> 01:17:29,620
After you, Dr. Kernitz.

1484
01:17:29,620 --> 01:17:30,730
- Thank you, Captain.

1485
01:17:30,730 --> 01:17:34,060
- [Crow] They're gonna
get tanked, tanked, Joel.

1486
01:17:34,060 --> 01:17:35,900
- [Joel] Good one, Crow.

1487
01:17:35,900 --> 01:17:38,503
- Dr. Kernitz and I have
rendezvoused with Yellow Fox.

1488
01:17:38,503 --> 01:17:40,726
ETA at the airport minus 20 minutes.

1489
01:17:40,726 --> 01:17:42,227
- Sig.

1490
01:17:42,227 --> 01:17:43,734
The Spectrum helicopter will over fly

1491
01:17:43,734 --> 01:17:45,920
the route to the airport.

1492
01:17:45,920 --> 01:17:48,800
And Angel aircraft will escort
your plane to cloud base.

1493
01:17:48,800 --> 01:17:50,483
- SIG, Leftenant Green.

1494
01:17:53,590 --> 01:17:55,020
- Very ingenious.

1495
01:17:55,020 --> 01:17:57,810
We can fly in comfort
and complete secrecy.

1496
01:17:57,810 --> 01:17:58,643
- That's right, Doctor.

1497
01:17:58,643 --> 01:18:01,090
Spectrum have found the tank very useful.

1498
01:18:01,090 --> 01:18:02,540
- [Joel] Kind of like a Yugo.

1499
01:18:03,860 --> 01:18:05,793
Comfort and complete secrecy.

1500
01:18:09,793 --> 01:18:11,220
Well, maybe.

1501
01:18:11,220 --> 01:18:12,740
- [Crow] You know, we
could use another countdown

1502
01:18:12,740 --> 01:18:13,907
right about now.

1503
01:18:21,600 --> 01:18:25,170
- Well, Doctor, what are
the results of your tests?

1504
01:18:25,170 --> 01:18:27,290
- I know the danger you
went through Captain Scarlet

1505
01:18:27,290 --> 01:18:29,240
to get the pulsator,

1506
01:18:29,240 --> 01:18:32,000
but I can tell you know it was worth it.

1507
01:18:32,000 --> 01:18:33,836
Because of your efforts,
I believe we will be able

1508
01:18:33,836 --> 01:18:37,200
to communicate with the Mysterons.

1509
01:18:37,200 --> 01:18:39,217
Let's hope they will listen to reason.

1510
01:18:40,086 --> 01:18:44,086
- [Mysteron] This is the
voice of the Mysterons.

1511
01:18:44,993 --> 01:18:48,160
We know that you can hear us earthmen.

1512
01:18:50,454 --> 01:18:52,704
Our next act of retaliation

1513
01:18:53,782 --> 01:18:56,282
will be to destroy cloud base.

1514
01:18:58,540 --> 01:18:59,540
Do you hear?

1515
01:19:00,689 --> 01:19:04,044
Spectrum's headquarters cloud base

1516
01:19:04,044 --> 01:19:06,544
will be destroyed at midnight.

1517
01:19:10,607 --> 01:19:12,707
- [Servo] Joel, you never moved your lips.

1518
01:19:18,310 --> 01:19:21,673
- Well, Colonel, the Mysterons
plan to destroy cloud base.

1519
01:19:21,673 --> 01:19:23,270
- Yes, Captain.

1520
01:19:23,270 --> 01:19:25,710
It's incredible they
should choose such a time.

1521
01:19:25,710 --> 01:19:28,370
But as this base is already
on maximum security alert.

1522
01:19:28,370 --> 01:19:30,530
There's very little more that we can do.

1523
01:19:30,530 --> 01:19:33,000
Except to ensure that
security arrangements

1524
01:19:33,000 --> 01:19:34,130
are carried out.

1525
01:19:34,130 --> 01:19:35,240
- Yes, Colonel.

1526
01:19:35,240 --> 01:19:37,910
- No one will be allowed to
leave or board cloud base.

1527
01:19:37,910 --> 01:19:39,890
And the entire craft will be subjected

1528
01:19:39,890 --> 01:19:42,400
to hourly searches with
Mysteron detectives.

1529
01:19:42,400 --> 01:19:43,930
- This is already being done, sir.

1530
01:19:43,930 --> 01:19:44,790
- Good.

1531
01:19:44,790 --> 01:19:46,870
Any plane, rocket or satellite approaching

1532
01:19:46,870 --> 01:19:49,850
within a 50-mile radius will be attacked.

1533
01:19:49,850 --> 01:19:50,857
The only exceptions to this

1534
01:19:50,857 --> 01:19:52,810
are the aircraft bringing Dr. Kernitz

1535
01:19:52,810 --> 01:19:54,573
and Captain Scarlet to cloud base.

1536
01:19:58,910 --> 01:20:00,294
- Spectrum have done a good job

1537
01:20:00,294 --> 01:20:02,700
on the transmission circuits, Colonel.

1538
01:20:02,700 --> 01:20:03,622
- Thank you, Doctor.

1539
01:20:03,622 --> 01:20:05,734
- It was built exactly
to the circuit diagrams

1540
01:20:05,734 --> 01:20:08,690
you sent us and it's been fully tested.

1541
01:20:08,690 --> 01:20:10,253
- Well, let's get on with it.

1542
01:20:16,610 --> 01:20:17,980
- Allow me doctor.

1543
01:20:17,980 --> 01:20:19,623
- [Dr. Kernitz] Certainly, Captain.

1544
01:20:29,230 --> 01:20:30,180
- [Captain] Did it.

1545
01:20:31,060 --> 01:20:34,340
- Good, switch on the primary seconds.

1546
01:20:34,340 --> 01:20:35,173
- Right.

1547
01:20:38,280 --> 01:20:39,113
- Pulsating.

1548
01:20:40,200 --> 01:20:41,797
Just as it did on the Mysteron complex

1549
01:20:41,797 --> 01:20:43,060
on the moon.

1550
01:20:43,060 --> 01:20:44,650
- Yes, Captain Blue.

1551
01:20:44,650 --> 01:20:45,870
With the aid of the photographs,

1552
01:20:45,870 --> 01:20:47,140
you can Captain Scarlet took,

1553
01:20:47,140 --> 01:20:49,100
it was relatively easy to assimilate

1554
01:20:49,100 --> 01:20:52,000
the exact conditions inside that complex.

1555
01:20:52,000 --> 01:20:53,560
- Is it going to work Doctor?

1556
01:20:53,560 --> 01:20:55,530
- I am certain it will.

1557
01:20:55,530 --> 01:20:56,790
Give me a couple of hours

1558
01:20:56,790 --> 01:20:58,090
to check the secondary circuits

1559
01:20:58,090 --> 01:21:00,270
and the frequency and for the first time,

1560
01:21:00,270 --> 01:21:02,821
you Colonel White will
be able to speak directly

1561
01:21:02,821 --> 01:21:04,507
to the Mysterons.

1562
01:21:04,507 --> 01:21:07,257
(dramatic music)

1563
01:21:12,720 --> 01:21:14,230
- What time is it, Leftenant.

1564
01:21:14,230 --> 01:21:16,550
- [Leftenant Green] 1100 hours, sir.

1565
01:21:16,550 --> 01:21:18,790
- 13 hours to midnight.

1566
01:21:18,790 --> 01:21:20,360
- [Leftenant Green]
Captain Blue is here here.

1567
01:21:20,360 --> 01:21:22,010
- Anything to report Captain Blue?

1568
01:21:22,010 --> 01:21:23,664
- Have the Mysteron
detectives revealed anything?

1569
01:21:23,664 --> 01:21:25,150
- No, Colonel.

1570
01:21:25,150 --> 01:21:26,810
The whole base has been checked out

1571
01:21:26,810 --> 01:21:28,410
and except for the diamond pulsator,

1572
01:21:28,410 --> 01:21:29,760
of course, there's nothing.

1573
01:21:29,760 --> 01:21:30,610
- The Mysteron said they

1574
