01:35:15,514 --> 01:35:18,573
- A trap. But why, why?

1829
01:35:20,270 --> 01:35:23,093
So much energy in one tiny pulsator.

1830
01:35:24,943 --> 01:35:28,460
The pulsator, the attack on cloud base.

1831
01:35:28,460 --> 01:35:29,988
I must warn them.

1832
01:35:29,988 --> 01:35:33,892
- [Crow] Hmm, things a
marionette might say, hmm.

1833
01:35:33,892 --> 01:35:36,642
(dramatic music)

1834
01:35:49,740 --> 01:35:51,417
- What time is it Leftenant?

1835
01:35:52,380 --> 01:35:53,980
- Five minutes to midnight, sir.

1836
01:36:05,826 --> 01:36:09,154
(tires squealing)

1837
01:36:09,154 --> 01:36:11,904
(dramatic music)

1838
01:36:24,740 --> 01:36:26,873
- It's got to work.

1839
01:36:34,090 --> 01:36:37,160
- Colonel, I've picked
up some sort of signal.

1840
01:36:37,160 --> 01:36:38,200
It's Morse.

1841
01:36:38,200 --> 01:36:39,853
- Morse? Let me hear it.

1842
01:36:40,780 --> 01:36:45,593
S, c, a, r, l.

1843
01:36:46,670 --> 01:36:47,570
It's from Scarlet.

1844
01:36:50,241 --> 01:36:53,250
He says the pulsator's
a Mysteron booby trap.

1845
01:36:53,250 --> 01:36:54,310
- 30 seconds to midnight, sir.

1846
01:36:54,310 --> 01:36:56,690
- Captain Oko, this is an emergency.

1847
01:36:56,690 --> 01:36:58,220
Do exactly as I say.

1848
01:36:58,220 --> 01:36:59,740
Take the diamond pulsator

1849
01:36:59,740 --> 01:37:01,611
to the nearest porthole and jettison it.

1850
01:37:01,611 --> 01:37:02,580
- Sig.

1851
01:37:02,580 --> 01:37:03,413
- [Colonel White] There will be

1852
01:37:03,413 --> 01:37:05,230
an explosive decompression in the room.

1853
01:37:05,230 --> 01:37:06,480
Put on a respirator.

1854
01:37:06,480 --> 01:37:08,001
- 15 seconds left, sir.

1855
01:37:08,001 --> 01:37:09,874
- Hurry Captain Oko.

1856
01:37:09,874 --> 01:37:11,372
- Ten.

1857
01:37:11,372 --> 01:37:12,205
Nine.

1858
01:37:12,205 --> 01:37:13,038
(glass exploding)

1859
01:37:13,038 --> 01:37:13,958
Eight.

1860
01:37:13,958 --> 01:37:14,791
Seven.

1861
01:37:14,791 --> 01:37:15,624
- [Servo] Hmm, nothing
like a good countdown.

1862
01:37:15,624 --> 01:37:17,080
- [Leftenant Green] Six.

1863
01:37:17,080 --> 01:37:18,342
Five.

1864
01:37:18,342 --> 01:37:19,941
- [Servo] That's what I often say.

1865
01:37:19,941 --> 01:37:20,774
- [Joe] I know.

1866
01:37:20,774 --> 01:37:21,616
- Three.

1867
01:37:21,616 --> 01:37:23,227
Two.

1868
01:37:23,227 --> 01:37:24,060
One.

1869
01:37:25,040 --> 01:37:28,123
(pulsator exploding)

1870
01:37:34,550 --> 01:37:36,350
- Firstly, I must thank
you Captain Scarlet

1871
01:37:36,350 --> 01:37:37,910
and you Captain Oko.

1872
01:37:37,910 --> 01:37:42,070
Because of your initiative,
cloud base is safe.

1873
01:37:42,070 --> 01:37:44,500
Well, gentlemen, the events of yesterday

1874
01:37:44,500 --> 01:37:46,203
can now be viewed in retrospect.

1875
01:37:47,050 --> 01:37:48,740
Our attempt to end the war of nerves

1876
01:37:48,740 --> 01:37:51,020
with the Mysterons has failed.

1877
01:37:51,020 --> 01:37:52,390
Obviously we were unable to convince them

1878
01:37:52,390 --> 01:37:56,073
of our sincerity, but we will try again.

1879
01:37:56,950 --> 01:37:58,830
Let us learn from this operation

1880
01:37:58,830 --> 01:38:00,980
and steal ourselves for the long road

1881
01:38:00,980 --> 01:38:02,704
which lies in front of us.

1882
01:38:02,704 --> 01:38:03,942
- [Joel] He's right, you know.

1883
01:38:03,942 --> 01:38:07,398
(dramatic music)

1884
01:38:07,398 --> 01:38:09,981
(upbeat music)

1885
01:38:28,239 --> 01:38:30,822
(upbeat music)

1886
01:38:34,470 --> 01:38:36,173
- [Joel] Jackie Gleason again.

1887
01:38:38,080 --> 01:38:40,491
- [Crow] That's the planet Earth, Joel.

1888
01:38:40,491 --> 01:38:43,160
- [Joel] Well, what'd you
think of the movie, Crow?

1889
01:38:43,160 --> 01:38:48,160
- [Crow] Well, I, uh, I
have some laundry to do.

1890
01:38:49,770 --> 01:38:51,235
- [Joel] You have laundry to do.

1891
01:38:51,235 --> 01:38:54,453
- [Crow] Now I do if you know what I mean.

1892
01:38:55,510 --> 01:38:56,931
- [Joel] What about you, Servo?

1893
01:38:56,931 --> 01:38:58,860
- [Servo] Well, it made me laugh,

1894
01:38:58,860 --> 01:39:01,563
but most of all, it made me cry.

1895
01:39:02,900 --> 01:39:03,733
- [Joel] That's good.

1896
01:39:03,733 --> 01:39:06,100
I wish I would have-
- [Servo] It made me think.

1897
01:39:06,100 --> 01:39:07,710
- [Joel] Oh, yeah, is that right?

1898
01:39:07,710 --> 01:39:09,160
- [Servo] It made me reflect.

1899
01:39:11,030 --> 01:39:13,940
- [Joel] I wish we could
have seen the Mysterons.

1900
01:39:13,940 --> 01:39:14,773
They never showed them, you know.

1901
01:39:14,773 --> 01:39:16,580
- [Servo] That made me think, too.

1902
01:39:16,580 --> 01:39:17,994
- [Crow] That's why there were Mysterons

1903
01:39:17,994 --> 01:39:19,600
because we never saw them.

1904
01:39:19,600 --> 01:39:20,433
- [Joel] I suppose.

1905
01:39:20,433 --> 01:39:21,482
- [Servo] That made me wonder.

1906
01:39:21,482 --> 01:39:23,669
- [Crow] Ran out of their
special effects budget.

1907
01:39:23,669 --> 01:39:26,610
- [Joel] Yeah, they saved on
actors if they could have-

1908
01:39:26,610 --> 01:39:28,506
- [Crow] Puppetry coordinator,
puppetry supervision.

1909
01:39:28,506 --> 01:39:33,408
- [Joel] That made me mad.

1910
01:39:33,408 --> 01:39:35,960
Whoa, lots of character
voices in that one.

1911
01:39:35,960 --> 01:39:38,280
- [Servo] Well, time for
me to drain my radiator.

1912
01:39:38,280 --> 01:39:39,244
- [Joel] Okay, see you around.

1913
01:39:39,244 --> 01:39:41,060
- [Servo] See you up in the front thing.

1914
01:39:41,060 --> 01:39:42,455
- [Joel] Okay.

1915
01:39:42,455 --> 01:39:43,860
We should get going, too, Crow.

1916
01:39:43,860 --> 01:39:46,080
- [Crow] That's right, I
have to get some things done.

1917
01:39:46,080 --> 01:39:48,530
- Yeah, go do your puppet laundry.

1918
01:39:49,845 --> 01:39:52,428
(upbeat music)

1919
01:40:41,958 --> 01:40:44,541
(logo buzzing)

1920
01:40:47,313 --> 01:40:49,896
(door banging)

1921
01:40:53,170 --> 01:40:54,415
All right, I'm really excited.

1922
01:40:54,415 --> 01:40:57,190
I just heard that Gypsy and Servo found

1923
01:40:57,190 --> 01:40:59,630
some turkey in the cargo bay.

1924
01:40:59,630 --> 01:41:00,700
- Here he comes now.

1925
01:41:00,700 --> 01:41:02,118
He said before we eat, we must observe

1926
01:41:02,118 --> 01:41:03,931
one Thanksgiving custom of earth.

1927
01:41:03,931 --> 01:41:05,777
- Oh, right, to give thanks.

1928
01:41:05,777 --> 01:41:07,800
- Make that two Thanksgiving customs,

1929
01:41:07,800 --> 01:41:10,680
to give thanks and to
pass the Chex party mix.

1930
01:41:10,680 --> 01:41:12,233
- All right, okay.

1931
01:41:13,200 --> 01:41:14,310
Thanks.

1932
01:41:14,310 --> 01:41:15,143
- Enjoy Joel Hodgson.

1933
01:41:15,143 --> 01:41:16,081
- Golly.

1934
01:41:16,081 --> 01:41:18,129
- And Crow, you, too.

1935
01:41:18,129 --> 01:41:20,540
- Well, never mind.
- Enjoy.

1936
01:41:20,540 --> 01:41:22,123
- Hmm, here's some for later.

1937
01:41:24,111 --> 01:41:25,295
- Here Crow, I'll give you some.

1938
01:41:25,295 --> 01:41:26,128
- I'm out of here.

1939
01:41:26,128 --> 01:41:27,313
Did you get some?

1940
01:41:28,420 --> 01:41:29,850
- Tasty.

1941
01:41:29,850 --> 01:41:32,390
- Oh, here comes Gypsy with
the main course, all right.

1942
01:41:32,390 --> 01:41:33,823
Hot turkey and...

1943
01:41:35,450 --> 01:41:37,140
Wait a minute, this isn't the kind

1944
01:41:37,140 --> 01:41:39,290
of turkey and gravy we have on earth.

1945
01:41:39,290 --> 01:41:40,123
- Moo?

1946
01:41:40,123 --> 01:41:41,300
- This stuff's in tubes.

1947
01:41:41,300 --> 01:41:43,096
- What do you expect on a
communication satellite?

1948
01:41:43,096 --> 01:41:45,730
Now, do you want dark meat, white meat

1949
01:41:45,730 --> 01:41:46,968
or winter fresh gel.

1950
01:41:46,968 --> 01:41:47,970
- Winter fresh gel.

1951
01:41:47,970 --> 01:41:50,400
- You're right, you're right, I know.

1952
01:41:50,400 --> 01:41:51,470
I should be thankful.

1953
01:41:51,470 --> 01:41:54,050
At least I have someone, I mean something

1954
01:41:54,050 --> 01:41:55,640
to spend Thanksgiving with.

1955
01:41:55,640 --> 01:41:56,473
- Yes.

1956
01:41:58,060 --> 01:41:59,330
- What are these crackers.

1957
01:41:59,330 --> 01:42:01,901
- Oh, the box said something
like soilant green.

1958
01:42:01,901 --> 01:42:04,050
Said it's made from people.

1959
01:42:04,050 --> 01:42:05,540
- Oh, they're good, though.

1960
01:42:05,540 --> 01:42:07,446
Mine shaped like Edward G. Robinson.

1961
01:42:07,446 --> 01:42:08,279
(all laughing)

1962
01:42:08,279 --> 01:42:09,830
We'll be right back with a movie.

1963
01:42:11,200 --> 01:42:12,093
That's good.

